			<Placemark>
				<name>Berri Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Berri, also blended into Arab Extra Light | API: ~38-39° | Sulfur: low (light sweet by Gulf standards)
Benchmark: Saudi Aramco Official Selling Price, set monthly against the Oman/Dubai average for Asia, against ICE Brent for Europe and against ASCI for the US
Operator: Saudi Aramco
Role: A field straddling the coast near Jubail producing one of Aramco&apos;s two low-sulfur grades alongside Arab Super Light — comparable in quality to a North African crude
Dual role: Berri is sold under its own name to Asian buyers, AND blended with Abqaiq crude and rising Shaybah output to make Arab Extra Light
Export route: Gathering to Abqaiq, then Ras Tanura and Ju&apos;aymah on the Gulf, or west via the East-West Pipeline to Yanbu
Risks: Mature field; its volumes are split between two competing uses, standalone sales and the Extra Light blend</description>
