				<name>Asab Oil Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Murban | API: ~40.3° | Sulfur: ~0.78% (light sour)
Benchmark: ICE Murban Futures (IFAD), physically delivered FOB Fujairah — launched 2021 as a rival to Brent and Dubai for Asian buyers
Operator: ADNOC Onshore
Role: One of the four onshore fields whose output forms Murban, alongside Bab, Bu Hasa and Sahil — a mature Abu Dhabi producer in the desert interior
Export route: Gathered at Habshan, then west to Jebel Dhanna or east via the ADCOP pipeline to Fujairah, bypassing the Strait of Hormuz
Risks: Field maturity requiring pressure support; processing concentration at Habshan</description>
