			<Placemark>
				<name>Satah Al Razboot (SARB) Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Blended into Umm Lulu | API: 38.7-39° | Sulfur: 0.7% (light sweet)
Benchmark: Sold within the Umm Lulu stream against Dubai
Operator: ADNOC Offshore — ADNOC 60%, Cepsa 20%, OMV 20%
Role: The second field of the Umm Lulu/SARB concession, developed with two purpose-built ARTIFICIAL ISLANDS — SARB North and SARB South — off the north-west coast of Abu Dhabi
Why blended: ADNOC combined SARB and Umm Lulu crude specifically to improve production, storage and export flexibility, creating one marketable grade rather than two small ones
Export route: Processing, storage and export at Zirku Island
Risks: Shares Umm Lulu&apos;s thin spot liquidity; artificial-island development carries high capital cost</description>
