			<Placemark>
				<name>Upper Zakum Oil Field (Offshore)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Upper Zakum | API: ~34° | Sulfur: ~1.7% (medium sour)
Benchmark: One of the FIVE deliverable grades in the Platts Dubai basket, alongside Dubai, Oman, Al-Shaheen and Murban — so Upper Zakum can directly set the Dubai price when it is cheapest to deliver
Operator: ADNOC Offshore — ADNOC 60%, ExxonMobil 28%, INPEX/JODCO 12%
Role: The world&apos;s second-largest offshore field, developed from four artificial drilling islands to cut cost and extend well reach
Capacity: Around 1 million b/d, targeting 1.2 million
Export route: Subsea lines to Zirku Island for processing and export — loading INSIDE the Gulf, unlike pipeline-served Murban
Strategic note: The contrast with Murban is the core of Abu Dhabi&apos;s supply-security story — Upper Zakum is Hormuz-exposed, Murban is not
Risks: Hormuz transit dependence; in-Gulf loading concentration at Zirku</description>
