				<name>Umm Shaif Oil Field (Offshore)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Das Blend | API: ~36.9° | Sulfur: ~1.1% (light sour)
Benchmark: ADNOC publishes a monthly Das Blend OSP against Dubai, alongside Murban, Upper Zakum and Umm Lulu
Operator: ADNOC Offshore
Role: Abu Dhabi&apos;s FIRST offshore discovery, found in 1958 — with Lower Zakum it forms the Das Blend export stream, processed on Das Island
Capacity: Around 275,000-300,000 b/d
Recent: A $6.2 billion gas cap development was approved in July 2026
Export route: Subsea pipelines to Das Island for processing, storage and tanker loading
Risks: Nearly seven decades of production; in-Gulf loading with Hormuz exposure; island-processing concentration</description>
