				<name>Gachsaran Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Iranian Heavy | API: 29.5° | Sulfur: 1.77% (heavy sour)
Benchmark: NIOC sets a monthly Official Selling Price against the Oman/Dubai average for Asia and against Dated Brent for Europe, published by Platts
Operator: National Iranian South Oil Company (NISOC)
Role: One of the giant Zagros foothill fields of Khuzestan and a core contributor to Iranian Heavy, Iran&apos;s largest export stream
Export route: Pipelines to Kharg Island for tanker loading
Refining note: Chinese teapots must blend Iranian Heavy with lighter grades before it can run through their distillation units, unlike Iranian Light which they crack directly
