				<name>Soroush Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Soroosh | very heavy sour, the heaviest Iranian export grade
Benchmark: NIOC publishes a monthly Soroosh OSP for Asia, consistently the deepest discount of the Iranian grades
Operator: Iranian Offshore Oil Company
Role: A heavy offshore field in the northern Persian Gulf, produced with the neighbouring Nowruz structure
Blending note: NIOC struggled for years to sell Soroush and Nowruz crude on its own because of its density and sulfur. The solution was to blend it at Bahregansar with lighter Bahregansar crude AND South Pars condensate to create a marketable grade — the same diluent logic as Orinoco or Cold Lake, but using the country&apos;s own gas condensate
Risks: US sanctions confine sales largely to Chinese independent refiners; cargoes move via shadow-fleet tankers with ship-to-ship transfers, often relabelled as Malaysian origin</description>
