			<Placemark>
				<name>South Pars Field (condensate)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Liquids grade: South Pars Condensate | API: 58.4° | Sulfur: very low (ultra-light)
Benchmark: Sold against Dated Brent and regional condensate assessments; a splitter and petrochemical feedstock rather than refinery crude
Operator: Pars Oil and Gas Company, for National Iranian Oil Company
Role: The Iranian half of the world&apos;s largest gas field, shared with Qatar&apos;s North Field — mapped here for its condensate, not its gas. At 58.4° API it is among the lightest liquids traded anywhere, comparable to Qatar&apos;s LSC
Domestic use: Feeds the Persian Gulf Star condensate refinery at Bandar Abbas, and is also used as diluent to make heavy Soroush crude marketable
Export route: Assaluyeh on the Persian Gulf coast
Risks: US sanctions confine sales largely to Chinese independent refiners; cargoes move via shadow-fleet tankers with ship-to-ship transfers, often relabelled as Malaysian origin</description>
