				<Point>
					<coordinates>118.55,37.45,0</coordinates>
				</Point>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Liaohe Field (Liaoning)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Liaohe | API: ~24° | Sulfur: moderate (heavy, waxy)
Benchmark: Largely domestic; small export volumes were historically marketed by foreign partners alongside Xijiang crude
Operator: PetroChina
Role: China&apos;s third-largest field, in Liaoning province near Panjin — a heavy, waxy crude feeding northeastern refineries
Export history: Around 100,000 b/d of waxy Liaohe and Xijiang were once marketed internationally by Shell, Phillips and Texaco on behalf of Chinese producers, reaching Indonesia, Hawaii and the US West Coast; those flows have since largely stopped
Risks: Mature field with heavy oil requiring thermal recovery; almost no export market remains</description>
				<styleUrl>#default10</styleUrl>
