					<coordinates>122.07,41.12,0</coordinates>
				</Point>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Bozhong Fields (Bohai Sea)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Bozhong / Bohai heavy | medium to heavy crude
Benchmark: Domestic; Bohai crude is not a significant export stream
Operator: CNOOC
Role: The central Bohai Sea field cluster and the core of China&apos;s largest offshore production base — Bozhong 13-2 alone holds around 100 million tonnes of oil-equivalent in place, and the Bohai region accounts for roughly a third of CNOOC&apos;s output
Recent: Bozhong 19-6, a very large condensate gas field, started production in November 2023, adding light liquids to a region otherwise dominated by heavy crude
Strategic role: Bohai is where China&apos;s domestic production growth is concentrated, as state majors are directed to cut import dependence
Risks: Predominantly heavy crude needing thermal recovery; shallow, busy waters close to major cities</description>
