			<Placemark>
				<name>Qinhuangdao Fields (QHD 32-6, Bohai Sea)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Qinhuangdao / Bohai heavy | medium-heavy crude
Benchmark: Domestic refining feedstock
Operator: CNOOC, historically with foreign partners including BP, Shell and Phillips
Role: The northern Bohai field group, anchored by QHD 32-6 — one of the developments that opened the Bohai to international partnership in the early 2000s
Recent: CNOOC announced Qinhuangdao 27-3 in March 2024 and Qinhuangdao 29-6 later, each with over 100 million tonnes of proved in-place oil equivalent, both classified medium-heavy crude in the Shijiutuo Uplift
Strategic role: Part of the Bohai push to lift domestic output — China produced about 4.15 million b/d of crude in 2023 while importing roughly 11 million b/d
Risks: Heavy crude requiring thermal recovery; shallow water in a heavily trafficked sea</description>
