				<Point>
					<coordinates>-111.45,57.02,0</coordinates>
				</Point>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Hibernia Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Hibernia | API: 33.9-34.0° | Sulfur: 0.58-0.63% (medium light, low sulfur)
Benchmark: Priced against Dated Brent and WTI; ExxonMobil publishes a full public assay, and its very low metals — 1.4 ppm vanadium, 2.0 ppm nickel — and TAN under 0.1 make it an easy refinery feed
Operator: ExxonMobil Canada, with Chevron, Suncor, Canada Hibernia Holding and Equinor
Role: The anchor of Canada&apos;s east coast offshore, produced from a gravity-base concrete platform on the Grand Banks built to withstand iceberg impact
Export route: Shuttle tankers to the Whiffen Head transshipment terminal in Placentia Bay, then conventional tankers to market
Risks: North Atlantic ice and weather; a mature field on a harsh, remote shelf</description>
