			<Placemark>
				<name>White Rose Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: White Rose | API: 31° | Sulfur: 0.31% (medium, sweet)
Benchmark: Priced against Dated Brent and WTI; its low sulfur made it a natural fit for Ontario, Quebec and US East Coast refineries
Operator: Cenovus Energy, following the Husky Energy merger
Role: A Grand Banks field 350 km east of St. John&apos;s, producing since November 2005 from the SeaRose FPSO — the sweetest of the Newfoundland grades
Recent: The first cargo, about 600,000 barrels, went to Irving Oil&apos;s Canaport terminal in New Brunswick; later shipments went to the US Gulf Coast
Export route: Shuttle tankers to Whiffen Head, or direct to refineries on the east coast
Risks: Iceberg and storm exposure; FPSO-dependent with no pipeline alternative</description>
