			<Placemark>
				<name>Bakken (Williston Basin, North Dakota)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Bakken | API: ~42° | Sulfur: ~0.1-0.2% (light sweet)
Benchmark: Priced against WTI at Clearbrook and Guernsey; rail and pipeline netbacks to the Gulf Coast and East Coast set the differential
Operator: Continental Resources, ConocoPhillips, Hess, Marathon and others
Role: The shale play that first broke US production higher after 2008, in North Dakota and eastern Montana — light sweet crude with very low sulfur
Export route: Dakota Access Pipeline south to Patoka and the Gulf Coast; Enbridge&apos;s mainline east; crude-by-rail when pipeline space is tight
Risks: Pipeline capacity and legal challenges to Dakota Access; high decline rates requiring constant drilling</description>
