			<Placemark>
				<name>Permian Basin – Midland Basin</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: WTI Midland | API: ~42-44° | Sulfur: ~0.2% (light sweet)
Benchmark: Since June 2023, WTI Midland is a DELIVERABLE GRADE IN THE DATED BRENT BASKET — the first non-North Sea crude admitted, and frequently the cheapest-to-deliver, meaning Permian barrels now set the world&apos;s most-quoted benchmark
Operator: ExxonMobil, Chevron, Diamondback, Oxy, ConocoPhillips and others
Role: The core of the Permian and the single largest source of US light sweet crude
Export route: Long-haul pipelines to Corpus Christi, Houston and Nederland for export; also north to Cushing
Risks: Takeaway capacity cycles; water handling and gas flaring constraints</description>
