			<Placemark>
				<name>Permian Basin – Delaware Basin</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: WTI Midland | API: ~42-44° | Sulfur: ~0.2% (light sweet)
Benchmark: Feeds the same WTI Midland stream now deliverable into Dated Brent
Operator: ExxonMobil, Chevron, Coterra, Devon and others
Role: The western half of the Permian, straddling Texas and New Mexico — higher gas-oil ratios than the Midland side but the same light sweet crude quality
Export route: Gathering east and south into the Midland system and the Gulf Coast export lines
Risks: Gas takeaway limits can constrain oil production; New Mexico permitting</description>
