			<Placemark>
				<name>Eagle Ford Basin (South Texas)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Eagle Ford | API: ~47-52° (extra light, condensate-rich) | Sulfur: very low
Benchmark: Priced against WTI; its lightness makes it a splitter and petrochemical feedstock rather than a conventional refinery crude
Operator: ConocoPhillips, EOG, Marathon, Chesapeake and others
Role: The South Texas shale play, and the source of the lightest significant US crude stream — so light that much of it is closer to condensate than crude
Quality note: High naphtha yield suits petrochemical crackers, but its low middle-distillate content means refiners often blend it down rather than run it neat
Export route: Short pipeline runs to Corpus Christi, the shortest path from wellhead to water of any US shale play
Risks: Extreme lightness limits the buyer set; competes with Middle East condensate in Asian splitters</description>
