					<coordinates>-98.50000000000001,28.5,0</coordinates>
				</Point>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Prudhoe Bay Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Alaska North Slope (ANS) | API: ~31-32° | Sulfur: ~1.0% (medium sour)
Benchmark: Priced against ICE Brent and WTI; ANS is the reference crude for the US West Coast, where it competes with Colombian Vasconia and Latin American heavies
Operator: Hilcorp, which acquired BP&apos;s Alaska business in 2020
Role: The largest oil field ever discovered in North America, producing since 1977 and the anchor of the ANS blend
Export route: The Trans-Alaska Pipeline System 800 miles south to the Valdez Marine Terminal, then tanker to West Coast refineries
Risks: Decades of decline; TAPS needs minimum throughput to keep crude warm enough to flow through permafrost</description>
