				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Alaska North Slope (ANS) | API: ~31-32° | Sulfur: ~1.0% (medium sour)
Benchmark: Sold within the ANS stream against ICE Brent and WTI
Operator: ConocoPhillips Alaska
Role: North America&apos;s second-largest oil field by area, west of Prudhoe Bay — the other main contributor to the ANS blend
Export route: Into the Trans-Alaska Pipeline System and on to Valdez
Risks: Mature field requiring enhanced recovery; shares TAPS&apos; minimum-throughput problem</description>
