			<Placemark>
				<name>Mars–Ursa–Olympus Complex</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Mars | API: ~29.5° | Sulfur: ~1.89% (medium sour)
Benchmark: The most actively traded US Gulf sour grade, priced as a differential to WTI at Cushing — recently 70-80 cents/b under the benchmark
Operator: Shell
Role: The Mississippi Canyon platform group that defines the Mars stream — Mars, Ursa and Olympus, joined by Vito, all delivering to LOOP&apos;s Clovelly hub where Mars has dedicated underground cavern storage
Strategic role: Mars is the US medium sour reference, and a component of LOOP Sour alongside Poseidon. When hurricanes shut the Mars stream, refiners replace it with Urals, Saudi barrels or blended WCS
Risks: Hurricane exposure — Ida shut the stream entirely in 2021; ageing platform infrastructure</description>
