			<Placemark>
				<name>Thunder Horse Platform</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Thunder Horse | API: medium sour, slightly lighter than Mars
Benchmark: Priced as a differential to WTI Cushing, and notably trades at a PREMIUM — around 30 cents/b above the benchmark, where Mars sits 70-80 cents below
Operator: BP
Role: BP&apos;s flagship Gulf of Mexico development and the namesake of its own stream, with dedicated cavern storage at LOOP&apos;s Clovelly hub
Connectivity: Shell&apos;s Appomattox crude also markets as Thunder Horse, arriving via the Proteus and Endymion pipelines
Recent: BP&apos;s South Expansion Phase 2 added 25,000 boe/d feeding the platform
Risks: Hurricane exposure; deepwater operating complexity</description>
