				<name>Galeota Block (Trintes Field)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Galeota Mix | API: 40° (light sweet)
Benchmark: Priced against WTI and Dated Brent; Trinidad&apos;s main crude export grade
Operator: Trinity Exploration &amp; Production, with Heritage Petroleum holding an overriding royalty
Role: The core producing block off Trinidad&apos;s east coast, covering the producing Trintes field plus the Echo development and the Foxtrot and Golf appraisal areas
Licence: A new 25-year Galeota licence was issued in July 2021 over 19,280 acres, with reduced work obligations and a new crude oil sales agreement
Export route: Loaded at Galeota Point on the south-east tip of Trinidad
Context: National crude output has fallen to roughly 59,000-63,000 b/d, about half the 2006 level, and gas now dominates the country&apos;s energy sector
Risks: Small and declining production base; capital constrained; a light sweet grade competing against much larger Atlantic basin streams</description>
