			<Placemark>
				<name>Castilla Field (Meta)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Castilla Blend | API: 18-19° | Sulfur: ~2% (heavy sour)
Benchmark: Priced against WTI; marketed as an alternative to Mexican Maya as that grade declines, and bought by Asian and US Gulf refiners including Sinochem, ExxonMobil, Valero and Koch
Operator: Ecopetrol
Role: The anchor field of Colombia&apos;s heavy Llanos production and the namesake of Castilla Blend, which pools several Llanos heavy streams and cuts them with naphtha to make them pipelineable
Export route: Llanos gathering system into the OCENSA pipeline, then the Coveñas terminal on the Caribbean
Risks: Requires imported diluent to move; competes directly with Maya and Canadian heavy for the same US Gulf refineries</description>
