				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Feeds Castilla Blend | heavy, high viscosity
Benchmark: Sold within Castilla Blend against WTI
Operator: Ecopetrol, following the end of the Pacific Rubiales association
Role: Colombia&apos;s largest heavy-oil field, in the Llanos Basin near Puerto Gaitán, developed with Piriri alongside it — the volume behind the country&apos;s heavy export growth
Export route: A 230 km dedicated line to the Monterrey station, then OCENSA to Coveñas; built for 170,000 b/d and expandable to 280,000 b/d
Risks: Heavy crude needing dilution and pressure support; field maturity after years of intensive water injection</description>
