			<Placemark>
				<name>Medanito Field / Neuquén Basin (Vaca Muerta)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Medanito | API: 40.8° | Sulfur: 0.146% (light, very sweet)
Benchmark: Assessed by Argus FOB Argentina; Argentina&apos;s most sought-after grade, with Trafigura the largest single buyer
Operator: Multiple — YPF, Vista, Pluspetrol, Shell and others across Neuquén and Río Negro blocks
Role: The reference grade of the Neuquén Basin and the stream that carries Vaca Muerta shale oil to market
Quality note: 50.2% paraffins, total acid number under 0.1 and a −36°C pour point — a clean, waxy light crude with high naphtha and light-distillate yield
Export route: Oldelval pipeline east to Puerto Rosales and the Trafigura terminal at Puerto Galván, Bahía Blanca. The Vaca Muerta Sur line to Punta Colorada, around 30% built, will add VLCC loading from roughly 200,000 b/d rising toward 700,000 b/d by 2030
Recent: First cargoes to China in 2025; Trafigura has taken 1.4 million barrels a month from over 14 Vaca Muerta producers
Risks: Export capacity, not production, is the binding constraint until Vaca Muerta Sur is complete</description>
