			<Placemark>
				<name>Escalante Field (Golfo San Jorge, Chubut)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Escalante | API: ~24° | Sulfur: ~0.2% (heavy but sweet, high acidity)
Benchmark: Sold at a discount to light grades; valued by refiners with heavy-crude configurations
Operator: PRIO, which bought Equinor&apos;s 60% stake in 2025 to become sole operator, alongside other Golfo San Jorge producers
Role: The characteristic grade of the Golfo San Jorge Basin and Argentina&apos;s main heavy stream — the counterweight to Medanito in the national export basket
Quality note: Low sulfur but high total acid number, so it needs refineries equipped for naphthenic acid corrosion
Export route: Termap terminal at Caleta Córdova, near Comodoro Rivadavia
Recent: Around 30% of Escalante exports went to the US in early 2025, second only to Spain at 50%; cargoes are increasingly combined with Medanito on a single Suezmax loading at two ports
Risks: Mature fields in long-term decline; heavy-crude discount; a narrower buyer pool than Medanito</description>
