				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Cañadón Seco | API: ~26-27° | Sulfur: low (medium-heavy, sweet)
Benchmark: Priced alongside Escalante as a Golfo San Jorge heavy stream, at a discount to Medanito
Operator: YPF and Santa Cruz basin partners
Role: The southern Golfo San Jorge counterpart to Escalante, marketed as its own grade rather than blended with it — slightly lighter, from the Santa Cruz side of the basin
Export route: Termap terminal at Caleta Olivia, a separate loading point from Escalante&apos;s Caleta Córdova
Strategic role: Argentina keeps its two Golfo San Jorge streams apart, each with its own terminal, rather than pooling them into one heavy blend
Risks: Mature conventional fields; provincial fiscal terms; competes for capital against Vaca Muerta</description>
