				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Mero | API: ~29° | Sulfur: low (medium sweet)
Benchmark: Priced against Dated Brent
Market: Brazilian pre-salt crude sells overwhelmingly to China, where independent &apos;teapot&apos; refiners value its heavy gasoil yield and low sulfur; Petrobras cargoes have traded at a premium to Brent there
Operator: Petrobras 38.6%, Shell 19.3%, TotalEnergies 19.3%, CNOOC 9.65%, CNPC 9.65%, PPSA 3.5%
Role: The main development of the Libra block in the Santos pre-salt, and one of Brazil&apos;s newer export streams — first cargoes went to Chinese refiners after test production began in 2017
