				<description>Status: Operational — first oil 2025
Crude grade: Bacalhau | API: ~28-30° | Sulfur: low (medium sweet)
Benchmark: Priced against Dated Brent; a new addition to Brazil&apos;s pre-salt slate
Market: Brazilian pre-salt crude sells overwhelmingly to China, where independent &apos;teapot&apos; refiners value its heavy gasoil yield and low sulfur; Petrobras cargoes have traded at a premium to Brent there
Operator: Equinor 40%, ExxonMobil 40%, Petrogal Brasil 20%
Role: One of the largest pre-salt developments outside Petrobras operatorship, in the Santos Basin — produced through a purpose-built FPSO
