				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Roncador Heavy | API: ~18-20° | Sulfur: moderate (heavy)
Benchmark: Priced against Dated Brent at a discount reflecting its density — a different buyer set from the pre-salt grades
Operator: Petrobras, with Equinor holding a significant stake acquired in 2018
Role: A giant Campos Basin field and one of Brazil&apos;s largest producers before the pre-salt era — it produces several streams, of which Roncador Heavy is the separately marketed heavy grade
Strategic note: Represents the OLD Brazil — post-salt Campos Basin heavy crude, in contrast to the light sweet Santos pre-salt barrels that now dominate exports
