				<name>Peregrino Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Peregrino | API: ~13-14° | Sulfur: moderate, with high acidity (heavy)
Benchmark: Priced against Dated Brent at a steep discount; a niche heavy grade for refiners equipped to handle high-TAN crude
Operator: Equinor, which acquired full operatorship after previously sharing the asset with a Chinese partner
Role: A heavy-oil field in the Campos Basin roughly 85 km off Rio de Janeiro, produced from fixed platforms with an FPSO — Brazil&apos;s heaviest commercially exported crude
