			<Placemark>
				<name>ITT Field (Ishpingo–Tambococha–Tiputini, Block 43)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational — subject to a 2023 referendum mandating phased shutdown
Crude grade: Napo | API: ~18.8-19.2° | Sulfur: ~2.0-2.1% (heavy sour)
Benchmark: Napo is the heavy sour grade, priced against WTI; comparable in gravity to Mexican Maya and aimed at US Gulf Coast refiners configured for heavy sour feed
Operator: Petroecuador
Role: Ecuador&apos;s largest heavy-oil development, inside Yasuní National Park in the eastern Amazon — the field the country counted on to lift national output toward 700,000 b/d
Export route: The OCP heavy-crude pipeline to Balao, kept separate from SOTE so its density does not degrade Oriente
Recent: A 2023 national referendum voted to halt production in Block 43, creating long-running uncertainty over Ecuador&apos;s heavy-crude volumes
Risks: Legal mandate to wind down; environmental and indigenous-rights opposition; Napo volumes depend heavily on this one block</description>
