			<Placemark>
				<name>Liza Field / FPSO Station</name>
				<description>Status: Operational — first oil December 2019
Crude grade: Liza | API: 32° | Sulfur: 0.58% (medium sweet)
Benchmark: Assessed by Platts and Argus against the Latin America Dated Brent strip, ICE Brent and WTI, on FOB cargoes of 1 million barrels
Operator: ExxonMobil Guyana 45%, Chevron 35% (acquired from Hess), CNOOC 20%
Role: Guyana&apos;s first producing development, on the Stabroek Block — the project that turned a country with no oil industry into a major Atlantic basin supplier in under a decade
Capacity: Produced from the Liza Destiny FPSO, the first of the block&apos;s vessels
Export route: Loaded directly from the FPSO to tankers; cargoes go mainly to Europe and North America, with the US now among the largest buyers
Risks: Entirely offshore and FPSO-dependent; Venezuela disputes sovereignty over the neighbouring Essequibo region</description>
