			<Placemark>
				<name>Boscán Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Boscán | API: 10.1° | Sulfur: 5.4% (extra-heavy, extremely sour)
Benchmark: Deep discount to Dated Brent; a niche asphalt-grade crude
Operator: Petroboscán — PDVSA 60%, Chevron 39.2%
Capacity: ~100,000 b/d, producing since 1947 in Zulia, south-west of Maracaibo
Quality note: Too viscous to flow unaided, and its ~11,222 ppm vanadium — over 40× Merey — destroys refinery catalysts without heavy pre-treatment. Used mainly for asphalt
Export route: Loaded at Bajo Grande, Zulia, and by ship-to-ship transfer off Amuay
Recent: Chevron lost its export licence in March 2025; PDVSA now markets the crude, with cargoes going to Malaysia for transshipment to China after decades of US-only sales
Risks: Sanctions dictate the buyer pool; very few refineries can process it</description>
