			<Placemark>
				<name>Mesa Field (Mesa 30)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Mesa 30 | API: 30.1° | Sulfur: 1.04% (light, medium sour)
Benchmark: Priced against Dated Brent — one of Venezuela&apos;s few streams sold on quality rather than discount
Operator: PDVSA
Role: Source of Mesa 30, from the Oficina area of Anzoátegui, and the country&apos;s scarcest resource: light crude
Dual use: Orinoco crude at 8-10° API cannot be shipped without lighter oil blended in, and Mesa 30 is that diluent. Every barrel used to make Merey 16 is one denied to domestic refineries
Export route: Jose terminal and Puerto la Cruz; cargoes also go to Cuba and Curaçao
Recent: Diverting Mesa 30 abroad left the 187,000 b/d Puerto la Cruz refinery running at 16% of capacity
Risks: Falling light-crude output forces PDVSA to import diluent</description>
