			<Placemark>
				<name>Bomu Oil Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Bonny Light | API: ~35.1° | Sulfur: ~0.15% (light sweet)
Benchmark: Assessed against the West Africa Dated strip (Dated Brent-linked); Nigeria&apos;s flagship grade and an OPEC reference crude. Its very low sulfur and low corrosiveness make it a premium feedstock for European and US refiners
Operator: Renaissance Africa Energy (took over SPDC&apos;s onshore joint venture from Shell in March 2025)
Role: An Ogoniland field and the head of the Trans Niger Pipeline — the point where Bonny Light&apos;s western gathering system begins
Export route: Trans Niger Pipeline via Rumuekpe to the Bonny terminal, then the Bonny CLP offshore loading buoys
Recent: An explosion at Bodo in Gokana LGA in March 2025, shortly after Renaissance completed its takeover from Shell
Risks: Oil theft and illegal tapping along the Ogoniland route; long-running community and environmental disputes; repeated force majeure history</description>
