				<name>Nembe Field Area (OML 29)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Bonny Light | API: ~35.1° | Sulfur: ~0.15% (light sweet)
Benchmark: Assessed against the West Africa Dated strip (Dated Brent-linked); Nigeria&apos;s flagship grade and an OPEC reference crude. Its very low sulfur and low corrosiveness make it a premium feedstock for European and US refiners
Operator: Aiteo Eastern E&amp;P, with NNPC, TotalEnergies and Eni as partners
Role: The Bayelsa production area at the head of the Nembe Creek Trunk Line — the second of the two arteries feeding Bonny Light
Export route: Nembe Creek Trunk Line via Cawthorne Channel to the Bonny terminal
