			<Placemark>
				<name>Hassi Berkine (HBNS) Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Saharan Blend | API: ~45° | Sulfur: ~0.1% (very light, very sweet)
Benchmark: Sonatrach sets a monthly official price for Saharan Blend against Dated Brent — recently around a 40 cents/b PREMIUM, one of the few crudes in the region to price above the marker and the direct competitor to Libya&apos;s El Sharara
Operator: Sonatrach with Occidental Petroleum (formerly Anadarko) under a production-sharing association
Role: The anchor of the Berkine Basin in eastern Algeria — the discovery that revived Algerian oil output in the 1990s and the largest single addition to Saharan Blend since Hassi Messaoud
Export route: Gathering lines north-west to Haoud El Hamra, then the trunk system to Bejaia and Skikda on the Mediterranean, or by the OK1 line
Risks: Mature Berkine production; foreign-partner contract terms have been a recurring point of friction with Sonatrach</description>
