			<Placemark>
				<name>Sharara Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational — repeatedly shut by blockades and force majeure
Crude grade: El Sharara | API: ~43° | Sulfur: ~0.07% (very light, very sweet)
Benchmark: NOC sets a monthly official price against Dated Brent, recently around a 70 cents/b discount; its closest regional competitor is Algeria&apos;s Saharan Blend
Operator: Akakus Oil Operations — NOC with Repsol, TotalEnergies, OMV and Equinor
Role: Libya&apos;s largest oil field at around 300,000 b/d, in the Murzuq Basin of the south-west — the single biggest contributor to national output
Export route: Roughly 750 km of pipeline north to the Zawiya terminal on the Mediterranean, west of Tripoli
Recent: Among the most frequently halted assets in Libya, shut by tribal blockades, militia action and force majeure on numerous occasions since 2011
Risks: Its remote desert location makes the pipeline vulnerable along its whole length; output swings of 300,000 b/d move global balances</description>
