			<Placemark>
				<name>Sarir Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Sarir | API: ~38° | Sulfur: moderate
Benchmark: NOC monthly official price against Dated Brent — historically the DEEPEST discount of the Libyan grades, around $3.95/b below the marker, reflecting its heavier quality
Operator: Arabian Gulf Oil Company (AGOCO), a NOC subsidiary
Role: The largest onshore field in eastern Libya, in the Sirte Basin — the anchor of the eastern production system
Export route: Pipeline east to Marsa el Hariga at Tobruk, with some volumes to Ras Lanuf
Strategic note: Sarir and Mesla are the heavy end of the Libyan slate, and their wider discount shows how much Libya&apos;s premium depends on lightness and sweetness rather than volume
Risks: Eastern Libya&apos;s contested political control; repeated port closures at Hariga</description>
