				<name>Bu Attifel Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Bu Attifel | API: ~43° | Sulfur: very low, but VERY HIGH WAX
Benchmark: NOC monthly official price against Dated Brent, recently around a 55 cents/b discount
Operator: Mellitah Oil &amp; Gas — NOC and Eni
Role: An eastern Sirte Basin field whose crude is light and sweet but exceptionally waxy
Technical note: Bu Attifel and Zueitina crude must be continuously stirred and heated or they solidify in tanks and pipelines. NOC has reported tank leaks at Zueitina caused by accumulating solid wax, and has struggled to store the grade during periods of underfunded maintenance
Export route: Pipeline to the Zueitina terminal on the Gulf of Sirte
Risks: Wax handling makes storage and shutdowns unusually costly; Zueitina has been under force majeure repeatedly</description>
