			<Placemark>
				<name>Bouri Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Bouri | SOUR — one of only two sour grades Libya exports, alongside Al-Jurf
Benchmark: NOC monthly official price against Dated Brent, recently around a $1.35/b discount
Operator: Mellitah Oil &amp; Gas — NOC and Eni
Role: The largest offshore oil field in the Mediterranean, roughly 120 km off north-west Libya — producing since 1988 from fixed platforms
Export route: Loaded directly at the offshore Bouri terminal via a floating storage vessel, never reaching Libyan shore
Strategic note: Bouri is the exception in a country known for light sweet crude — its sour quality means it prices and sells into a different refinery set entirely
Risks: Ageing offshore infrastructure; Mediterranean maritime security; its sour quality limits the buyer pool relative to Libya&apos;s other grades</description>
