			<Placemark>
				<name>Azadegan Oil Field (North &amp; South)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational (development well below potential)
Crude grade: West Karun blend / Iran Heavy | API: ~29.5° and below | Sulfur: high (heavy sour)
Benchmark: NIOC official pricing, against Platts Dubai / DME Oman
Operator: NIOC via Petroleum Engineering and Development Company (PEDEC)
Role: Iran&apos;s largest oil discovery in decades (~33 billion barrels in place, ~5.2 billion recoverable) and the anchor of the West Karun cluster near the Iraqi border — NIOC planned a dedicated &quot;West of Karun&quot; heavy grade around these fields
Export route: Pipelines to Kharg Island
Risks: Severely under-produced relative to reserves due to sanctions blocking foreign investment and technology; shares a reservoir with Iraq&apos;s Majnoon across the border, creating a competitive-drainage dynamic; Hormuz dependence</description>
