			<Placemark>
				<name>Majnoon Oil Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Basrah Medium | API: ~27.9° | Sulfur: ~3.0% (medium/heavy sour)
Benchmark: SOMO Official Selling Price, against Platts Dubai / DME Oman
Operator: Basra Oil Company (nationalised operatorship after Shell&apos;s 2018 exit)
Role: One of the world&apos;s largest undeveloped fields by reserves (~13 billion barrels); SOMO has marketed dedicated Basrah Medium cargoes specifically against Basra Oil Company&apos;s Majnoon entitlement
Export route: Pipelines to Fao, then ABOT
Risks: Hormuz dependence; underinvestment relative to reserve size; regional security</description>
