			<Placemark id="072AC446C03F2D28A0C3">
				<name>Taq Taq oil field</name>
				<description>Status: Offline
Crude grade: Kurdistan Blend (KBT), light component — historically among the lightest Kurdish streams | API: ~30-32° blend | Sulfur: ~2.7% (medium sour)
Benchmark: When flowing, marketed against Dated Brent at Ceyhan
Operator: Genel Energy (operator, historically ~44% — exit terms agreed with the KRG January 2025); historic partners Sinopec/Addax ~36%, KRG ~20%
Role: Once the largest internationally operated field in Kurdistan and, with Tawke, one of the two light-crude pillars of the Kurdistan export blend
Capacity: Peaked at 116,000 b/d in 2015; fell on geological complications and reserve downgrades to under 5,000 b/d before the 2023 pipeline closure, then to zero — no production in 2024
Export route: Historically into the KRG line at Fishkhabur to Ceyhan; currently none
Risks: No restart plan or confirmed operator; reserve downgrades; its decline is a key reason the Kurdistan blend struggled to hold its quality</description>
