			<Placemark id="07C24C13813F39F143AC">
				<name>Tawke oil field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Kurdistan Blend (KBT), light component | API: ~30-32° blend | Sulfur: ~2.7% (medium sour)
Benchmark: Marketed via SOMO since the September 2025 Baghdad-KRG agreement, priced against Dated Brent at Ceyhan — historically sold at steep discounts to Dated Brent given the legal dispute over Kurdish exports
Operator: DNO ASA 75% (operator); Genel Energy 25%
Role: Tawke + Peshkabir complex — with Taq Taq, one of the two light-crude mainstays that define the Kurdistan export blend; gas capture and reinjection at Peshkabir roughly halves its emissions intensity
Capacity: 2025 average ~70,100 boe/d, ~77,300 by Q4; target 100,000 boe/d
Export route: Feeds the KRG export line at Fishkhabur, into the Iraq-Türkiye Pipeline to Ceyhan — a Mediterranean route independent of Hormuz
Recent: Ramp-up resumed February 2026 after a 30-month drilling hiatus; shut as a precaution 13 March 2026 amid regional war after drone strikes in July 2025; KRG pipeline flows resumed 18 March
Risks: Drone strikes (installations hit three times in 2025); war-related shutdowns; payment mechanism; licence renewal to 2031/2036</description>
				<LookAt>
					<longitude>42.79620380482646</longitude>
					<latitude>37.13612164673467</latitude>
