				<name>Ahdab Oil Field ( Al-Waha Petroleum Company)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Contributes to the Basrah blend (heavier component) | API: ~27-31° | Sulfur: ~2.7-3.0% (medium sour)
Benchmark: SOMO Official Selling Price, against Platts Dubai / DME Oman
Operator: Al-Waha Petroleum Company (CNPC-led)
Role: One of the first post-2003 fields developed under a Chinese contract; cited by SOMO among the newer, heavier sources that shifted Iraqi grade quality
Export route: Pipelines to the southern export system at Fao/ABOT
Risks: Hormuz dependence for exports; central Iraq location with associated security exposure</description>
