				<name>East Baghdad Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational (limited development)
Crude grade: Heavy sour, largely used domestically rather than exported as a named grade | API: ~22-25° | Sulfur: high
Benchmark: Not separately assessed; domestic refinery feedstock
Operator: Midland Oil Company (Iraqi state)
Role: A large but heavily under-developed field beneath and around Baghdad — development constrained for decades by its urban location and by security conditions
Export route: Primarily to domestic Iraqi refineries rather than the Basrah export system
Risks: Urban encroachment limiting drilling; chronic underinvestment; security</description>
