			<Placemark>
				<name>Greater Burgan Oil Field</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Kuwait Export Crude (KEC) | API: ~30.2° | Sulfur: ~2.7% (medium sour)
Benchmark: KPC Official Selling Price, set monthly against the Platts Dubai / DME Oman average for Asia
Operator: Kuwait Oil Company (KOC)
Role: The world&apos;s second-largest conventional oil field and the core of the Kuwait Export Crude blend — roughly 1.6 million b/d, the bulk of Kuwaiti production
Export route: Gathering centres north to Mina Al-Ahmadi terminal for Gulf loading
Risks: Multi-decade maturity; a 2021 fire at the field (without production loss) highlighted surface-facility risk; Hormuz dependence</description>
