				<description>Status: Operational
Liquids grade: Condensate joining the Vityaz / Sakhalin Blend export stream | very light, low sulfur
Benchmark: Sold within the Sakhalin Blend stream against Dubai for Asian buyers
Operator: Sakhalin Energy — Gazprom ~77.5% (absorbed Shell&apos;s 27.5% stake in 2022); Mitsui 12.5%; Mitsubishi 10%
Role: Sakhalin-2&apos;s gas leg, ~15 km off north-east Sakhalin Island — the single Lun-A platform feeds the onshore processing facility and the Prigorodnoye LNG plant; mapped here for its condensate, which joins the crude export stream
Capacity: Over 50 million m3/day of gas; ~16,000 b/d of exportable condensate
Export route: Trans-Sakhalin pipeline south to Prigorodnoye
