				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: ARCO (Arctic Oil) | API: ~24° | Sulfur: high (heavy sour)
Benchmark: Sold against Dated Brent at a discount reflecting its heavy sour quality; a niche grade suited to refiners configured for heavy feedstock
Operator: Gazprom Neft Shelf
Role: Russia&apos;s ONLY offshore oil production platform in the Arctic — a gravity-based ice-resistant structure standing on the Pechora Sea floor, producing since December 2013
Capacity: Ramped from 2.6 million t/yr in 2017 toward a planned peak around 5 million t/yr
Export route: Ice-class shuttle tankers to the Umba floating storage vessel in Kola Bay, then larger tankers onward — historically to Rotterdam
Strategic role: Proof of concept for Arctic offshore production, and one of the two fields that made the Kola Bay transshipment chain necessary
Risks: Extreme Arctic offshore conditions; sanctions on Arctic technology and shipping; heavy sour crude with a narrow buyer pool</description>
