				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: CPC Blend | API: ~45° blend | Sulfur: ~0.55% (light sour blend; this field&apos;s own stream is light and sweet)
Benchmark: Sold within CPC Blend against Dated Brent; CPC&apos;s internal quality bank pays a premium for lighter, sweeter streams, so this crude earns more than it would blended into Urals
Operator: LUKOIL
Role: The largest oil field in the Russian sector of the Caspian and the biggest single Russian contributor to CPC Blend — discovered 2005, on stream October 2016, Russia&apos;s largest oil discovery in 25 years
Capacity: Plateau of 6 million t/yr (~120,000 b/d) since 2018; recoverable reserves ~129 million tonnes
Export route: Subsea pipeline to onshore storage, then into the CPC system to Novorossiysk; associated gas goes to LUKOIL&apos;s Stavrolen petrochemical plant
Recent: Production halted in July 2026 after a Ukrainian drone attack on the platform — part of the same campaign that has repeatedly struck the CPC marine terminal
Risks: Drone-attack exposure; ice-resistant platforms in shallow Caspian water; complete dependence on the CPC corridor</description>
