				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Novy Port | API: ~30-35° | Sulfur: ~0.1% (medium gravity, VERY sweet)
Benchmark: Sold against Dated Brent; its extremely low sulfur makes it a premium Arctic grade, though post-2022 it has been discounted heavily to reach Chinese and Indian buyers
Operator: Gazprom Neft
Role: The source of the Novy Port grade, on the Yamal Peninsula — one of the sweetest crudes Russia produces, at roughly a tenth the sulfur of Urals
