				<description>Status: Operational
Crude grade: Urals | API: ~31-32° | Sulfur: ~1.3-1.4% (medium sour, this field&apos;s own stream is heavier and sourer)
Benchmark: Russia&apos;s flagship export blend and the reference for medium sour crude in Europe; priced at a discount to Dated Brent, widened sharply by post-2022 sanctions and the G7 price cap
Operator: Tatneft
Role: The giant Tatarstan field discovered in 1948 that anchored Soviet production before West Siberia was developed; its heavy, high-sulfur crude is a main reason the Urals blend is as sour as it is
Capacity: In production for over 75 years, now deep in decline and sustained by enhanced recovery
Export route: Transneft network to the Baltic and Black Sea, and into Druzhba toward Belarus and central Europe
