				<Placemark>
					<name>Bajo Grande Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: PDVSA (originally built 1956 by Richmond, now Chevron)
Capacity: 16,000 b/d — dedicated specifically to ASPHALT production
Role: The third refining unit of the Paraguaná Refinery Complex (with Amuay and Cardón), though physically located here on Lake Maracaibo&apos;s western shore in Zulia rather than on the Paraguaná Peninsula
Feedstock: Boscán and other extra-heavy, high-vanadium crude — precisely the grade best suited to asphalt rather than fuel production
Location: Verified at 10°30&apos;31.40&quot;N, 71°38&apos;27.40&quot;W
Connectivity: Sits ~3.6 km inland from its own dedicated loading jetty on the coast
Risks: Small, specialised, single-product refinery; feedstock tied to Boscán&apos;s own sanctions-affected output</description>
