				<Placemark>
					<name>CEPSA Gibraltar-San Roque Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: CEPSA
Capacity: 240,000 b/d — Spain&apos;s largest refinery, at San Roque on the Bay of Algeciras, right at the Strait of Gibraltar
Role: Directly receives crude via its own port facilities — one of Europe&apos;s most strategically placed refineries, sitting on the chokepoint between the Atlantic and Mediterranean and next to Algeciras, one of Europe&apos;s busiest bunkering and transshipment ports
Risks: Strait of Gibraltar traffic congestion; high-value strategic location increases geopolitical exposure</description>
