				<Placemark>
					<name>Repsol Bilbao Refinery (Petronor)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Repsol
Capacity: 220,000 b/d — at Muskiz on Spain&apos;s north Atlantic coast, Basque Country
Feedstock: Receives crude directly via its own coastal import facilities, including regular Venezuelan cargoes — Repsol&apos;s CEO has stated the firm receives about two tankers a month of Venezuelan crude here
Role: The main refining hub for northern Spain
Risks: North Atlantic weather exposure; feedstock diversification tied to sanctions-sensitive Venezuelan supply</description>
