				<Placemark>
					<name>Repsol Cartagena Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Repsol
Capacity: 220,000 b/d — on the Mediterranean coast, following a major expansion that made it one of Repsol&apos;s most complex, highest-conversion plants
Feedstock: Receives crude directly via its own Mediterranean port facilities, including Venezuelan cargoes — three arrived in a single month in 2019, some loaded at the Jose terminal already on this map
Role: Connected to the inland Puertollano refinery by Spain&apos;s main crude pipeline (357 km) — the two plants effectively operate as one integrated system
Risks: Feedstock exposure to sanctioned Venezuelan supply; high capital intensity of its conversion units</description>
