				<Placemark>
					<name>Jose Upgrading Complex (PetroPiar, PetroCedeño, PetroMonagas, Petro San Félix)</name>
					<description>Status: Reduced
Type: Four extra-heavy upgraders on one coastal complex — the technology built to turn 8 API tar into light synthetic crude
Operator: PDVSA JVs; PetroPiar (Chevron) the functional flagship
Capacity: ~600,000+ b/d combined nameplate upgrading capacity
Current reality: TRUE upgrading is largely DORMANT — the syncrude grades these plants were built to produce (Cerro Negro, Hamaca, Zuata Sweet, Morichal 16) have not shipped since 2017-2019, when sanctions and underinvestment shut most trains down. Most of the complex now runs in BLENDING-ONLY mode instead
Crude grades: Extra-heavy in from the Faja; MEREY 16 out — Venezuela&apos;s only currently-traded Orinoco grade, made by dilution rather than full upgrading
Role &amp; connections: Fed by the Faja-Jose Crude &amp; Diluent Corridor; feeds the Jose tank farms and terminal
Agreement note: Restoring full upgrading is the framework&apos;s biggest single industrial task — $100bn investment ambition VERIFIED as stated, allocation UNCONFIRMED
Source: Reuters/AP Aug 2026; industry assessments</description>
