				<Placemark>
					<name>Ecopetrol Barrancabermeja Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Ecopetrol (state-owned)
Capacity: 250,000 b/d — Colombia&apos;s LARGEST refinery, inland in Santander department on the Magdalena River
Feedstock: Crude arriving via the OCENSA/national pipeline grid, including Cusiana, Rubiales and Castilla streams already on this map
Role: The country&apos;s oldest major refinery, dating to the 1920s oil boom that first put Barrancabermeja on the map; still the anchor of Colombia&apos;s inland fuel supply
Recent: Integrated with Cartagena under Ecopetrol&apos;s SIR (Sistema Integrado de Refinación), launched 2022, to synchronise national gasoline and diesel production; has suffered occasional shutdowns from power outages and past sabotage
Risks: A single large refinery for the country&apos;s interior; ageing units alongside newer capacity at Cartagena</description>
