				<Placemark>
					<name>Ecopetrol Cartagena Refinery (Reficar)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Ecopetrol (state-owned)
Capacity: ~200,000 b/d — Colombia&apos;s second-largest, on the Caribbean coast at Cartagena, after a 2022 project integrated the original 50,000 b/d unit with the modern 150,000 b/d Reficar complex (completed 2015, ~$8 billion)
Role: A flagship modernisation project built to cut Colombia&apos;s low-sulfur fuel imports and raise export-quality product output; coastal location gives it direct access to both crude imports and product exports
Recent: Part of the same SIR integration scheme as Barrancabermeja, aiming to sync national refining output and reduce reliance on imported diesel and gasoline
Risks: One of the most capital-intensive refinery projects in Colombian history — high fixed-cost base sensitive to margin cycles</description>
