				<Placemark>
					<name>Repsol La Pampilla Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Repsol
Capacity: 117,000 b/d — Peru&apos;s LARGEST refinery, at Ventanilla, Callao, on the coast north of Lima
Feedstock: A mix of imported crude (arriving via the adjacent Callao import terminal) and domestic crude shipped up the coast from Bayóvar
Role: Supplies most of the Lima metropolitan area, Peru&apos;s largest fuel market
Recent: Ran at just 30% of capacity during the 2020 COVID demand collapse, illustrating how import-dependent and demand-sensitive Peru&apos;s refining sector is
Risks: Heavy reliance on imported crude; a single refinery dominating national capacity</description>
