				<Placemark>
					<name>Petroperu Talara Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Petroperu (state-owned)
Capacity: ~95,000-115,000 b/d — Peru&apos;s second-largest, on the far north coast in Piura, near the historic Talara oilfields
Role: Modernised under the PMRT (Talara Refinery Modernisation Project) to process heavier, higher-sulfur crude and cut fuel imports — Petroperu&apos;s flagship refining asset
Feedstock: Declining local Talara-area production plus jungle crude arriving via the ONP pipeline and Bayóvar
Risks: The PMRT project ran far over budget and schedule, straining Petroperu&apos;s finances; feedstock supply tied to the ONP&apos;s frequent shutdowns</description>
