				<Placemark>
					<name>Petroperu Iquitos (Loreto) Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Petroperu
Capacity: ~12,000 b/d — an isolated refinery deep in the Amazon jungle at Iquitos, Loreto
Feedstock: NOT connected to the ONP pipeline or the national grid — crude reaches it by RIVER BARGE from nearby jungle fields (Blocks 8, 67, 192), since no road or pipeline links Iquitos to the rest of Peru
Role: Supplies fuel to the entire isolated Peruvian Amazon region, which has no other practical fuel source
Why it matters: A vivid illustration of Amazon logistics — the same river-dependent isolation seen at Brazil&apos;s Urucu, but here serving a refinery rather than just a producing field
Risks: Total dependence on river transport; seasonal water-level constraints; serves a market with no alternative supply</description>
