				<Placemark>
					<name>PetroChina Guangdong Petrochemical Jieyang Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operational since February 2023
Owner: PetroChina (CNPC)
Capacity: 400,000 b/d (20 Mt/yr) — at Jieyang, Guangdong, southern China; ~$9.2 billion
Configuration: Integrated refining-petrochemical complex — 1.2 Mt/yr ethylene, 2.6 Mt/yr aromatics; equipped with a 2-million-barrel VLCC berth and product jetties
Role: One of the newest large Chinese coastal complexes, built to serve southern-China demand and the liquids-to-chemicals strategy
Why here: At the 400k mark — Standard tier
Risks: Weak domestic petrochemical margins at start-up; feedstock import dependence</description>
