				<Placemark>
					<name>Nayara Energy Vadinar Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Nayara Energy — a consortium led by Russia&apos;s Rosneft and a Trafigura/UCP group (formerly Essar Oil)
Capacity: 401,000 b/d — at Vadinar, Gujarat, western India, on the Gulf of Kutch near Reliance&apos;s Jamnagar
Role: India&apos;s second-largest single-site refinery after Jamnagar; exports products and supplies a large domestic retail network
Notable: Its Rosneft ownership has made it a significant processor of discounted Russian crude since 2022, and a focus of sanctions attention
Why here: Just above 400k, below the mega line — Standard tier
Risks: Sanctions exposure via Russian ownership and Russian-crude sourcing; margin and feedstock-access risk</description>
