					<name>Pemex Tula Refinery (Miguel Hidalgo)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Pemex (Petroleos Mexicanos), state-owned
Capacity: 340,000 b/d — in Hidalgo state, central Mexico, and often Pemex&apos;s highest-throughput plant (led the system at ~263,000 b/d in April 2026)
Recent: A new coking unit came online July 2025, raising throughput ~39,000 b/d and cutting low-value fuel oil
Role: Supplies the huge Mexico City market; landlocked, fed by crude pipeline from the Gulf
Risks: Air-quality scrutiny near Mexico City; ageing units alongside the new coker</description>
