Owner: Pemex (Petroleos Mexicanos), state-owned
Capacity: 285,000 b/d — in Veracruz on the Gulf coast, supplying southern Mexico and the Yucatan
Feedstock: Heavy Maya and Isthmus crude
Risks: A 2025 fire cut output; heavy-crude processing constraints</description>
