					<name>Marathon Los Angeles Refinery (Carson–Wilmington)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Marathon Petroleum
Capacity: 365,000 b/d — California&apos;s LARGEST refinery, ~25% of state crude capacity
Location: Carson/Wilmington, Los Angeles basin
Configuration: The Carson and Wilmington plants were merged into one reporting entity in 2019, linked by pipeline into an integrated complex
Feedstock: ANS (Alaskan North Slope) and waterborne imports, plus California heavy crude; makes CARB gasoline and diesel to California&apos;s unique specs
Why it matters: The anchor of Southern California fuel supply as the region&apos;s refinery base shrinks around it
Risks: California regulatory pressure (minimum-inventory rules, profit-cap proposals); an isolated market with no large-pipeline crude supply</description>
