					<description>Status: Operational — running at only ~60% utilisation
Owner: Acelen, controlled by Mubadala Capital of Abu Dhabi
Capacity: 333,000 b/d — Brazil&apos;s second-largest and its OLDEST, commissioned 1950 with over 75 years of continuous operation; ~14% of national capacity
Location: São Francisco do Conde, Bahia
Units: Atmospheric and vacuum distillation, FCC, hydrodesulfurisation, distillate hydrotreating, hydrogen generation and sulfur recovery
History: Sold by Petrobras to Mubadala in November 2021 for $1.65 billion during the Bolsonaro government&apos;s divestment programme, and renamed Mataripe
Recent: President Lula said in March 2026 that Petrobras will seek to BUY IT BACK. Acelen is meanwhile investing R$736 million in 2026 and R$4 billion by 2030
Risks: Low utilisation while Petrobras&apos; own refineries run near full; ownership uncertainty pending any repurchase</description>
