				<Placemark>
					<name>Persian Gulf Star Refinery (Bandar Abbas)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational — three phases complete, a fourth announced
Owner: Persian Gulf Star Oil Company — Oil, Gas and Petrochemical Investment Company 49%, Oil Industry Pension Fund 33.1%, NIORDC 17.9%
Type: Condensate refinery, not a crude refinery — three 120,000 b/d splitters, three 78,000 b/d Axens naphtha hydrotreaters, LPG recovery and Merox units
Capacity: 360,000 b/d, the LARGEST gas condensate refinery in the world; built on 700 hectares 25 km west of Bandar Abbas at a cost of about $3.4 billion
Feedstock: South Pars condensate, roughly 450,000 b/d delivered by pipeline from Assaluyeh
Main products: About 42 million litres a day of gasoline and 14 million litres of diesel, plus kerosene and LPG — more than 45% of Iran&apos;s total fuel supply
Strategic role: Built explicitly to end Iran&apos;s gasoline imports. National Euro-4 gasoline output went from 3.4 million litres a day in 2013 to 54 million by 2018, a fourteen-fold rise driven largely by this plant
Risks: Depends entirely on one pipeline and one condensate source; sanctions limit product export options</description>
