				<Placemark>
					<name>Bapco Sitra Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Bapco Refining, state-owned
Capacity: 267,000 b/d, raised toward 360,000 b/d under the Bapco Modernisation Programme
Feedstock: Predominantly IMPORTED — 220,000-230,000 b/d of Saudi crude arrives by pipeline from Abqaiq, with only about one-sixth coming from Bahrain&apos;s own Awali field
Main products: LPG, naphtha, gasoline, jet fuel, diesel and fuel oil; naphtha goes to Asian petrochemical buyers and LPG is marketed with Banagas
Role: Bahrain&apos;s only refinery, operating since 1936 when it started at just 10,000 b/d — one of the oldest continuously running refineries in the Gulf
Strategic role: Refined products account for roughly three-quarters of Bahrain&apos;s total exports. The country&apos;s business model is buying Saudi crude, refining it, and selling products — a refining margin play rather than a resource play
Risks: Almost total dependence on Saudi crude supply and on the single AB pipeline; margin exposure rather than price exposure</description>
