				<Placemark id="077D626E7D40213C6606">
					<name>Equinor Mongstad Refinery, Industrial Site &amp; Crude Oil Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Refinery operated by Equinor; the Mongstad crude terminal (MTDA) is Equinor 65% / Norwegian state 35%, Equinor-operated
Capacity: ~180,000 b/d refining; ~9.44 million barrels of underground crude storage — ~40% of Equinor-operated Norwegian shelf oil is stored here before export
Feedstock: Norwegian North Sea crude (Johan Sverdrup, Troll, Gjøa, Kristin, Vega), mainly by pipeline
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, LPG, naphtha, gasoil, heavy fuel oil, sulphur, petcoke
Markets: Norway, Europe, North America, Asia — via the refinery and the adjacent crude-export terminal
Recent: Major maintenance shutdown 2025; a fatal lifting accident and a benzene-exposure incident led to stronger safety measures in 2026
Strategic role: Norway&apos;s only refinery and one of its most important crude-storage and marine-export hubs
Risks: North Sea weather; pipeline interruption; terminal congestion; outages; industrial accidents</description>
