				<Placemark id="040E9977C63FCC60F669">
					<name>Bayernoil Refinery – Neustadt/Vohburg</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: VAROPreem 51.43% (majority; VARO also acquired BP&apos;s Vohburg bitumen plant and BP&apos;s 9% stake in TAL), Rosneft Deutschland 28.57% (under German federal trusteeship since Sept 2022), Eni 20%
Capacity: Up to 10 Mt/yr (~200,000–210,000 b/d) across the two sites
Feedstock: Imported crude via the Transalpine Pipeline (TAL) from Trieste
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, heating oil, jet components, LPG, bitumen
Markets: ~half of Bavaria&apos;s fuel demand plus northern Austria; jet fuel to Munich airport
Recent: 2018 Vohburg explosion and fire (ten injured), restarted 2020; Jan 2025 fire at Neustadt (two injured), temporary disruption; 2025 environmental report confirms two-site operation
Strategic role: Bavaria&apos;s largest refining company and the physical junction of the TAL corridor (IKL to Czechia branches here)
Risks: Full dependence on Trieste/TAL; fires and outages; European energy and carbon costs; declining regional demand</description>
