				<Placemark>
					<name>Wesseling- refinery converting to base oils (2027)</name>
					<description>Status: Converting
Owner: Shell Deutschland
Capacity: Historical crude distillation ~147,000 b/d (ended March 2025); new Group III base-oil unit ~300,000 t/yr from 2027 — ~9% of EU and 40% of German base-oil demand, Germany&apos;s largest
Feedstock: Vacuum gasoil piped from the Godorf refinery; a 315,000 t/yr Shell steam cracker also operates on site
Main products: From 2027, Group III base oils for lubricants; petrochemical feedstocks
Recent: FID Jan 2024; crude distillation ceased March 2025; conversion columns erected Feb 2025; start-up 2027; ~620,000 t CO₂/yr Scope 1+2 cut via end of crude processing and electrification
Strategic role: A live case of refinery repurposing rather than closure — and a driver of the RMR pipeline&apos;s growing importance as regional crude runs decline
Risks: European base-oil overhang at launch; loss of local naphtha for the LyondellBasell crackers; first-of-its-kind execution</description>
