Owner: Midland Refineries Company (Iraqi Ministry of Oil)
Capacity: ~110,000 b/d nominal; historically often below, owing to ageing equipment and outages
Feedstock: Iraqi crude from central and northern fields via the national pipeline network
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, kerosene, jet components, LPG, fuel oil, naphtha, bitumen
Markets: Baghdad and central Iraq
Recent: Ongoing rehabilitation — power generation, reforming, diesel hydrotreating; an 18 MW gas-power unit restarted in 2024, improving electricity reliability
Strategic role: One of Iraq&apos;s oldest refineries, mainly hydroskimming — the principal refining asset serving Baghdad
Risks: Ageing infrastructure; low conversion; electricity failures; fires; pipeline interruptions; urban environmental impact</description>
