Feedstock: Historically crude; latterly intermediates and finished products
Main products: LPG, naphtha, gasoline, gasoil (historical)
Markets: Rotterdam and NW Europe
Recent: Operations halted late 2024 (no viable feedstock); July 2025 — plan to mothball Europoort terminal activities announced
Strategic role: Historically a small Rotterdam refinery and terminal — now positioned for conversion toward lower-carbon and sustainable-fuel activities
Risks: Permanent loss of refining; terminal mothballing; weak European margins; feedstock availability; transition-project delays; regulatory uncertainty</description>
