					<name>Mozyr Oil Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Belarusian state (Belneftekhim), with a substantial minority stake historically held by Russia&apos;s Slavneft
Capacity: ~12 Mt/yr (~240,000 b/d) nameplate; throughput below capacity since 2022 amid sanctions
Feedstock: Russian crude via the southern Druzhba branch
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, fuel oil, LPG, bitumen, petrochemical intermediates
Markets: Belarus; exports to Ukraine, the Baltics, Poland and Europe largely curtailed since 2022
Recent: Under EU, US, UK, Swiss, Canadian and Ukrainian sanctions since 2022; 2026 satellite reporting showed Russian-supplied air defences at the site (~30 km from the Ukrainian border); a 2024 storm forced a temporary outage
Strategic role: One of Belarus&apos;s two major refineries (with Naftan) — national fuel self-sufficiency and continued Russian-crude processing
Risks: Sanctions; loss of Western markets; proximity to the war; Druzhba dependence; parts and equipment access</description>
