					<name>Naftan Oil Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Belarusian state (99.83%, via Belneftekhim)
Capacity: ~12 Mt/yr (~240,000 b/d); a 2022 delayed-coking complex lifted processing depth to ~97.5%; ~$1.6bn modernisation by 2021
Feedstock: Russian crude via the northern Druzhba branch
Main products: Diesel, gasoline, fuel oil, LPG, bitumen, sulphur, petrochemical intermediates
Markets: Belarus; historical exports to Russia, Ukraine, the Baltics, the Netherlands and the UK — most Western outlets closed since 2021–22 sanctions
Recent: Sanctioned by the EU, US, UK, Switzerland, Canada and Ukraine (2021–22); the LLK-Naftan JV restructured as &quot;EddyTek&quot; to work around US sanctions
Strategic role: One of Belarus&apos;s two major refineries (with Mozyr) — critical to national supply and an outlet for Russian crude
Risks: Sanctions; loss of Western markets and technology; Druzhba dependence; workforce instability after the 2020 unrest</description>
