					<description>Status: Reduced
Owner: Rosneft (JSC Kuibyshev Refinery)
Capacity: ~7 Mt/yr (~140,000 b/d); part of Rosneft&apos;s three-refinery Samara hub with Novokuibyshevsk and Syzran; established 1945
Feedstock: West Siberian and Samara-region crude
Main products: Euro-5 gasoline and diesel, aviation kerosene, bitumen, LPG
Markets: Volga region and Russian domestic market
Recent: A drone strike on 10 June 2026 hit both primary crude units (CDU-4 and CDU-5, ~73,000 b/d each), forcing a full shutdown and fires; sister plants Syzran and Novokuibyshevsk also struck
Strategic role: One of three Rosneft refineries in the Samara hub — a major Volga-region fuel supplier
Risks: Drone attacks; prolonged outages; sanctions; replacement equipment and catalysts; fires</description>
