					<name>Yaya Oil Refinery (Yaysky NPZ)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: JSC NefteKhimServis (private, independent of Rosneft, Gazprom Neft and Lukoil)
Capacity: 3.3 Mt/yr primary (~66,000 b/d), plus 1.6 Mt/yr vacuum distillation and 0.7 Mt/yr hydrotreating; Phase 3 (delayed coking, ~98 bn roubles) under construction, targeting 2027
Feedstock: Crude and gas condensate delivered by rail
Main products: AI-92/95/98 gasoline, diesel, fuel oil, atmospheric gas oil
Markets: Kuzbass and West Siberia
Recent: Not among the Russian refineries hit by the Ukrainian drone campaign as of mid-2026 (over 4,000 km from Ukraine); Phase 3 on schedule
Strategic role: A significant independent refinery serving the Kuzbass coal and industrial region
Risks: Rail-logistics dependence; margin exposure without upstream production; Phase 3 execution; sanctions on Russian product exports</description>
