				<Placemark>
					<name>Dalian West Pacific Petrochemical Refinery — WEPEC</name>
					<description>Status: Operating

Owner/Operator: Dalian West Pacific Petrochemical Company — PetroChina-led joint venture with Chinese and international shareholders.

Capacity: 10 million tonnes of crude per year, approximately 200,000 barrels per day.

Feedstock: Designed primarily for imported medium and high-sulphur crude.

Main products: Gasoline, diesel, aviation kerosene, naphtha, LPG, polypropylene, benzene, mixed xylenes, sulphur, fuel oil and road asphalt.

Connectivity: Integrated with the Dayaowan–Xingang oil-terminal system, adjacent tank farms and Dalian’s pipeline, road and maritime distribution networks.

Strategic role: Dalian’s principal operating state-controlled refinery and an important alternative processing outlet following the shutdown of the old Dalian Petrochemical refinery.

Risks: Dependence on imported crude, exposure to maritime disruption and competition from newer, more deeply integrated refineries.</description>
