				<Placemark>
					<name>VTTI Fujairah Integrated Refinery &amp; Storage Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: VTTI; integrated with the Fujairah refinery and associated crude-processing operations
Role: Combined refining, crude processing, commercial storage, blending and marine-fuel production complex
Capacity: 1.943 million m³ of storage across 66 tanks; 100,000-b/d refinery and 80,000-b/d crude-processing units
Products: Crude, gasoline, naphtha, jet fuel, kerosene, gasoil, diesel, fuel oil, VGO, condensate and blending components
Marine access: Eleven jetty connections through the Port of Fujairah; maximum listed draft 16.5 metres
Strategic role: Converts imported crude and components into bunker fuels and other products while providing large captive and merchant storage inside the pricing hub
Risks: Refinery-storage co-location; dependence on port pipelines and manifolds; refining-margin and bunker-demand exposure</description>
