				<Placemark>
					<name>Slavneft-YANOS Yaroslavl Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Slavneft (joint venture of Rosneft and Gazprom Neft)
Capacity: ~15 Mt/yr (~300,000 b/d) — one of Russia&apos;s three largest refineries
Feedstock: Domestic crude via the Transneft network, arriving via the Ukhta-Yaroslavl trunk line; the refinery marks the literal starting point of the Baltic Pipeline System (BPS-1) toward Kirishi and Primorsk
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, base oils, aromatics, petrochemical feedstocks
Markets: Central Russia and the Moscow region; products also feed the Sever products pipeline toward Primorsk for export
Recent: A 2017 fire at a crude distillation unit killed one worker
Strategic role: The head of the Baltic Pipeline System — crude gathered here begins the ~1,000 km run to Primorsk that carries roughly a third of Russia&apos;s seaborne crude exports
Risks: Drone-attack exposure common to Russia&apos;s western refineries; single-corridor dependence for onward Baltic export; sanctions and equipment constraints</description>
