				<Placemark>
					<name>Hengli Petrochemical Dalian Refining and Petrochemical Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operating

Owner/Operator: Hengli Petrochemical / Hengli Group

Capacity: 20 million tonnes of crude per year, approximately 400,000 barrels per day; integrated with large ethylene, aromatics and PTA production capacity.

Feedstock: Primarily imported crude delivered by very large crude carriers.

Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, paraxylene, benzene, olefins and other petrochemical feedstocks.

Connectivity: Directly connected to Hengli’s captive 300,000-dwt crude berth, product berths, refinery tank farms and the wider Changxing Island petrochemical cluster.

Strategic role: One of China’s largest and most deeply integrated private refining complexes, combining crude processing with large-scale chemicals and polyester feedstock production.

Recent: The refinery continued operating after its owner was sanctioned by the United States in April 2026 over alleged Iranian crude transactions, which Hengli denies.

Risks: International sanctions and compliance exposure, dependence on seaborne crude and cyclical petrochemical margins.</description>
