				<Placemark>
					<name>BP Rotterdam Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: BP Raffinaderij Rotterdam B.V., wholly owned by BP
Role: Major integrated refinery in Rotterdam-Europoort; receives seaborne crude through Rotterdam’s deep-water oil infrastructure and converts it into gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, LPG and other petroleum products for the Northwest European market; the surrounding tanks provide integrated storage for crude feedstock, intermediate streams and finished products
Capacity: Approximately 400,000 b/d of crude-processing capacity across two roughly 200,000-b/d crude units, making it one of Europe’s largest refineries
Risks: Unplanned unit shutdowns and power failures; concentration of capacity in two large crude units; fire and spill exposure across extensive tankage; tightening European environmental regulation and long-term pressure on regional refining margins</description>
