				<Placemark>
					<name>Phillips 66 Lake Charles Refinery &amp; Integrated Tank Farm</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: Phillips 66
Role: Large, complex Gulf Coast refinery in Westlake, Louisiana. The extensive tank farm visible in the screenshot is integrated with the refinery and supports the receipt and storage of crude feedstock, buffering of intermediate refinery streams, product blending, and dispatch of gasoline, diesel and other refined products. It is commercially strategic to the Lake Charles refining and petrochemical cluster but is not part of the U.S. Strategic Petroleum Reserve
Capacity: 264,000 b/d of crude and total throughput; maximum production capability of approximately 105,000 b/d of gasoline and 115,000 b/d of distillates. Public information does not identify the contents or capacity of each individual storage tank
Risks: Gulf Coast hurricane, storm-surge and flooding exposure; fire, explosion and accidental-release hazards; dependence on regional pipeline, marine and power infrastructure; concentration within the Lake Charles refining and petrochemical corridor</description>
