				<Placemark>
					<name>CITGO Lake Charles Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: CITGO Petroleum
Role: Major high-complexity Gulf Coast refinery located at Sulphur, Louisiana, on the Calcasieu Ship Channel. The complex processes a diverse range of crude oils into gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, petrochemical feedstocks and other petroleum products. Its extensive integrated tank farms provide crude-feedstock, intermediate-stream and finished-product storage, while marine docks and regional pipeline connections support crude receipts and product distribution.
Capacity: Approximately 460,000 b/d of crude processing capacity, making it one of the largest refineries in the United States and the largest facility in CITGO’s refining network.
Risks: Gulf Coast hurricane, storm-surge and flooding exposure; fire and accidental-release hazards; dependence on the Calcasieu Ship Channel and regional pipeline infrastructure; high concentration of refining and petrochemical facilities in the Lake Charles corridor.</description>
