				<Placemark>
					<name>Sans titre - Repère</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: PetroKazakhstan Oil Products — 50/50 KazMunayGas and CNPC
Capacity: 6 million t/yr (~120,500 b/d); processed 6.23 Mt in 2025, Kazakhstan&apos;s largest refinery by throughput
Feedstock: Kumkol field group crude by pipeline; ran on Russian crude until the Kenkiyak–Kumkol link opened in 2009
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, LPG and fuel oil for southern Kazakhstan
Role: The newest of Kazakhstan&apos;s three refineries (1985) and the only one serving the populous south; a $1.8bn modernisation to 2018 raised refining depth from 73% to 88%
Recent: FEED work began February 2026 on doubling capacity to 12 million t/yr by 2030, at roughly $6 billion
Risks: Expansion depends on Chinese financing; feedstock tied to the maturing Kumkol fields</description>
