				<Placemark>
					<name>Hassi Messaoud refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Sonatrach
Capacity: ~22,000 b/d (~1.1 million t/yr) — one of Algeria&apos;s smallest refineries, ranking fifth of six
Feedstock: Hassi Messaoud crude taken directly from the adjacent field, the source of Saharan Blend
Main products: Gasoline, diesel and LPG for the southern Algerian domestic market
Role: A small topping refinery serving the oilfield town and surrounding Sahara region — it exists because trucking fuel 600 km south from the coastal refineries is uneconomic, not because the crude needs processing here
Recent: Sonatrach awarded a $3.7 billion EPC contract in 2020 to Técnicas Reunidas and Samsung Engineering for a new 5 million t/yr (~110,000 b/d) Euro-V refinery at Haoud El Hamra nearby, which would dwarf this plant
Risks: Small scale and simple configuration; its role is likely to shrink once the new Haoud El Hamra refinery starts up</description>
