				<Placemark>
					<name>Refinery Esmeralda</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: EP Petroecuador (state-owned)
Capacity: 110,000 b/d — Ecuador&apos;s largest refinery, ahead of La Libertad (45,000) and Shushufindi (20,000); Nelson complexity 6.36
Feedstock: Domestic Oriente crude arriving at the coast via the SOTE pipeline
Main products: Gasoline, diesel and fuel oil — roughly 65% of Ecuador&apos;s refined output
Role: The country&apos;s only conversion refinery, with an FCC unit at its core turning heavy fractions into gasoline and diesel; sits beside the Balao export terminal where SOTE and OCP both terminate
Risks: Ecuador still imports a large share of its fuel despite producing over 500,000 b/d of crude; recurring unplanned outages and ageing units</description>
