			<Folder>
				<name>Mega-refineries</name>
				<Placemark>
					<name>South Pars Gas Complex, Assaluyeh</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: South Pars Gas Company, for National Iranian Oil Company
Role: The onshore processing complex where South Pars production comes ashore — a line of phase-by-phase treatment trains, each called a &quot;refinery&quot; in Iranian usage, that strip condensate, LPG, ethane and sulfur out of the wet gas
Capacity: Produces around 710,000 barrels of gas condensate a day, Iran&apos;s entire condensate output
Distribution: About 450,000 b/d goes by pipeline to the Persian Gulf Star refinery at Bandar Abbas; volumes also feed the Nouri petrochemical plant and are exported as cargoes
Why it matters here: This is the point where the liquids separate from the gas. Everything downstream — Iran&apos;s gasoline self-sufficiency, the Soroosh blending programme, the condensate export trade — begins at these trains
Risks: Sanctions on equipment and technology; ageing phases needing pressure support as South Pars matures</description>
