				<Placemark>
					<name>Zhejiang Petroleum &amp; Chemical Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: Zhejiang Petroleum &amp; Chemical (ZPC)
Capacity: 40 Mt/yr—approximately 800,000 b/d
Feedstock: Predominantly imported Middle Eastern crude, supplemented by Canadian and other grades
Main products: Fuels, aromatics, olefins and petrochemical feedstocks
Strategic role: One of China’s largest and most modern refining-petrochemical complexes
Risks: Hormuz and Malacca exposure, typhoons, refinery margins and petrochemical overcapacity.</description>
