				<Placemark>
					<name>Amuay Refinery (CRP)</name>
					<description>Status: Reduced
Type: One half of the Paraguaná Refining Center — historically among the world&apos;s largest refineries
Operator: PDVSA
Capacity: 645,000 b/d NAMEPLATE; ACTUAL runs a small fraction, with chronic outages — the CRP as a whole has often run below 200,000 b/d combined in recent years (estimate)
Crude grades: Venezuelan and imported light/medium when available
Role &amp; connections: Domestic fuel supply above all — gasoline shortages track its breakdowns; Ule pipeline feed; own marine terminal
Recent: The 2012 explosion (55 dead) remains the emblem of its decline; flaring imagery from Jan 2026 accompanied this week&apos;s agreement coverage
Source: AP 30 Aug 2026 (imagery); EIA nameplate; run-rate estimates industry-derived</description>
