						<coordinates>-122.1105963985608,38.0174901524616,0</coordinates>
					</Point>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Neste Rotterdam Renewable Products Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational since 2011; major expansion under construction for expected completion in 2027
Operator: Neste Netherlands B.V., a subsidiary of Finland-based Neste Corporation
Role: Europe’s largest renewable-products refinery; uses Neste’s NEXBTL technology to convert waste oils, residual fats and other renewable feedstocks into HVO renewable diesel, sustainable aviation fuel (SAF) and renewable feedstocks for polymers and chemicals; integrated storage supports feedstock reception and finished-product distribution through Rotterdam
Capacity: 1.4 million tonnes/year of renewable products, including up to 500,000 tonnes/year of SAF; expansion targets 2.7 million tonnes/year of total renewable products and 1.2 million tonnes/year of SAF in 2027
Risks: Renewable-fuel oversupply and margin volatility; feedstock cost, availability and traceability; regulatory uncertainty; expansion delays, cost overruns and operational incidents</description>
