					<Point>
						<coordinates>-65.02901931678909,-41.69615914575756,0</coordinates>
					</Point>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Dos Bocas Marine Terminal (Tabasco)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Pemex (Petroleos Mexicanos), state-owned
Type: Onshore crude import/export terminal — tank farm and jetties, NOT an offshore buoy
Role: A key Gulf-coast crude export and import terminal in Tabasco, adjacent to the new Olmeca refinery — loads Mexican crude for export and handles product movements
Connectivity: Receives crude from the southern offshore fields and the Chiapas-Tabasco onshore fields; historically a major loading point for Isthmus and Maya crude
Note: As the Olmeca refinery ramps up, more crude that once exported from here is intended to be refined domestically instead
Risks: Weather exposure on the Gulf; shifting role as refining absorbs more crude</description>
