Former role: Britain&apos;s oldest refinery, opened by BP in 1924; 150,000 b/d capacity, around 14% of UK refining, supplying roughly 65% of Scotland&apos;s demand for refined products
Current role: Imports petrol, diesel, aviation fuel and kerosene via the Firth of Forth, with the existing tank farms repurposed as import storage; a £50 million conversion project
Connectivity: Still linked to the Forties Pipeline System via the neighbouring Kinneil terminal, and to Finnart Ocean Terminal on the Firth of Clyde by cross-country pipeline
