				<Placemark id="0B010FC4B63F23645016">
					<name>CPC Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Caspian Pipeline Consortium — Transneft (Russia, state trustee) 31%; KazMunayGas / Kazakhstan Pipeline Ventures ~20.75%; Chevron 15%; LUKARCO 12.5%; ExxonMobil (Mobil Caspian) 7.5%; Rosneft-Shell 7.5%; Eni 2%; Oryx 1.75%
Role: Marine export terminal at Yuzhnaya Ozereyevka near Novorossiysk — sea outlet of the 1,511 km CPC pipeline carrying Kazakh crude (Tengiz, Kashagan, Karachaganak) plus some Russian volumes to the Black Sea
Capacity: Three single point moorings (SPM) for offshore loading in poor weather; throughput being debottlenecked toward ~80 million t/yr (~1.6 million b/d); handles roughly 1.5% of global oil supply
Recent: Repeatedly struck by drone and tanker attacks through 2026, including a January strike disrupting Kazakh loadings and an April strike damaging an SPM and storage tanks — Kazakhstan has sought compensation given its near-total reliance on this one export route
Risks: War-related attack and blockage risk; single-corridor dependence for most Kazakh exports; weather-exposed offshore loading</description>
