					<name>Echo Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Enterprise Products Partners (ECHO — Enterprise Crude Houston)
Role: Crude storage and blending hub in Harris County, SE of Houston — links the Eagle Ford gathering system and the Seaway pipeline (from Cushing) into the Gulf Coast refining and export complex
Capacity: Built out to roughly 6 million barrels of crude storage across successive tank phases
Connectivity: Southern terminus of the Cushing–Houston corridor via Seaway; feeds Gulf Coast refineries and export docks; once weighed by CME/NYMEX as a Gulf Coast delivery point to unhook US benchmark pricing from landlocked Cushing
Risks: Exposed to Cushing/Permian supply swings; competition from newer Corpus Christi and Ingleside export terminals</description>
