				<Placemark id="06549B54963E92547180">
					<name>Primorsk Crude Oil Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Spetsmorneftport Primorsk LLC, a Transneft subsidiary; commissioned 27 December 2001
Role: Terminus of the Baltic Pipeline System (BPS-1), moving crude from the Timan-Pechora and West Siberian provinces (and some Kazakh volumes) to the Baltic
Capacity: ~65 million t/yr (~1 million b/d); 14 crude storage reservoirs; loads Russia&apos;s flagship Urals grade
Connectivity: The original Baltic bypass route, predating BPS-2/Ust-Luga by a decade; western Russia&apos;s largest port by cargo volume
Recent: Lost roughly 40% of storage capacity to Ukrainian drone strikes in March 2026 — at least 8 of its 50,000 m³ reservoirs were damaged
Risks: Repeated drone-attack exposure; central role in Russia&apos;s &quot;shadow fleet&quot; sanctions-evasion loadings, drawing continued targeting</description>
