				<Placemark id="07EFFEE8953E925D561B">
					<name>Ust-Luga Oil Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Built by Transneft subsidiary Nevskaya Truboprovodnaya Kompaniya; opened 2012
Role: Terminus of the Baltic Pipeline System-2 (BPS-2), a 1,000 km line from Unecha (Bryansk region) built to route Russian crude to the Baltic without transiting Belarus
Capacity: Tank farm of 8×50,000 m³ tanks; nameplate throughput ramped from 30 to ~38 million t/yr
Connectivity: Diverts crude previously exported via Novorossiysk/CPC on the Black Sea to the Baltic instead — part of the same strategic shift as Primorsk&apos;s BPS-1
Risks: Repeatedly struck by Ukrainian drone attacks since 2024, with loading suspensions in 2026; ice conditions in winter; single-corridor dependence on BPS-2</description>
