					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: ConocoPhillips (operator); TotalEnergies, Equinor and Eni hold non-operating interests
Role: Crude and NGL reception, processing, storage and export terminal at Seal Sands, Middlesbrough — UK landing point of the Norpipe subsea line from Norway&apos;s Ekofisk field, later joined by other North Sea tie-ins
Capacity: Original design capacity around 800,000 b/d; processes and stores the Ekofisk blend ahead of tanker export
Connectivity: The Ekofisk/Norpipe counterpart to Sullom Voe and Hound Point on the Forties/Ninian side of North Sea geography
Risks: Dependence on a single subsea import line; ageing infrastructure as connected fields mature</description>
