					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Mongstad Terminal DA (MTDA) — Equinor 65%, Norwegian State (Petoro) 35%; operated by Equinor
Role: Underground-cavern crude storage terminal at Mongstad, north of Bergen — distinct from but co-located with the Mongstad refinery; buffers Norwegian-shelf crude ahead of export
Capacity: 9.44 million barrels in underground rock caverns
Connectivity: Fed by an 83 km pipeline from Troll B/C and by Johan Sverdrup (since 2019); Norway&apos;s largest oil port by tonnage, exporting to North America, Europe and Asia
Risks: Concentrates a large share of Norwegian state-linked crude exports on one site; weather-exposed North Sea shipping lanes</description>
