					<name>Whiffen Head Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Newfoundland Transshipment Ltd (originally Mobil, Chevron and Petro-Canada); operated by International Matex Tank Terminals (IMTT)
Role: Transshipment terminal at Placentia Bay, Newfoundland — receives Grand Banks crude (Hibernia, Terra Nova and other fields) via purpose-built shuttle tankers, then reloads it onto conventional tankers for export
Capacity: Started with three 500,000-barrel tanks (1.5 million barrels) and one berth in 1998; expanded since with added tankage and a second berth
Connectivity: The sole aggregation point for Newfoundland&apos;s offshore oil before it reaches world markets
Risks: Harsh North Atlantic weather; single-site dependence for all Grand Banks crude exports</description>
