					<name>Corpus Christi storage terminal (USA)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Multiple third-party operators along the Corpus Christi Ship Channel and Harbor Island/Ingleside (including Moda Midstream/EPIC, South Texas Gateway, Enbridge Ingleside Energy Center, Buckeye Texas Partners)
Role: Crude storage and export terminal complex serving the Port of Corpus Christi — the largest US crude export gateway by volume, built almost entirely on Permian and Eagle Ford barrels moved south by pipeline
Capacity: Combined tens of millions of barrels of crude storage across the various operators&apos; tank farms
Connectivity: Terminus for multiple long-haul Permian pipelines; loads Aframax and Suezmax cargoes directly, VLCCs via reverse lightering, for export mainly to Asia and Europe
Risks: Hurricane exposure; channel-draft limits forcing partial VLCC loading offshore; concentrates a large share of US crude exports on the Texas Gulf Coast</description>
