				<Placemark>
					<name>Galeota Offshore Loading Point (approximate)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational — location APPROXIMATE, not visually verified
Owner/Operator: Trinity Exploration &amp; Production / Heritage Petroleum
Type: Almost certainly a single-point mooring (SPM) buoy — Galeota Point Terminal&apos;s own coastline faces open Atlantic swell (visible whitecaps on satellite imagery) with no jetty, and the nearby west-side port at Galeota is confirmed too small for tankers, ruling out a fixed berth
Why marked approximate: Satellite imagery resolution in this area is insufficient to visually confirm or precisely locate the actual buoy or mooring structure — this pin is placed a short distance offshore from the terminal, in the general direction of the Galeota Block field, as the most geographically reasonable estimate
Role: The final link completing Trinidad&apos;s short crude export chain — Galeota Mix loads here directly onto tankers, priced against WTI and Dated Brent
Full chain: Galeota Block (Trintes Field) → subsea gathering line → Galeota Point Terminal (onshore storage) → THIS offshore loading point → tanker export. No refinery step exists in this chain since Pointe-à-Pierre closed in 2018
Risks: Open Atlantic swell exposure typical of an unsheltered SPM site; location should be corrected if better imagery or a verified coordinate becomes available</description>
