Role: The floating production, storage and offloading vessel that is Sangomar&apos;s sole production and export point — named after Senegal&apos;s first president; Sangomar crude is sold FOB from this vessel
Facilities: Converted from a VLCC by MODEC in Singapore, then sailed 12,000 nautical miles to Senegal; 100,000 b/d capacity, 1.3 million bbl storage; moored ~100 km off Dakar
Why here: Senegal&apos;s inaugural offshore production facility, the physical anchor of the country&apos;s entry into the oil-exporting world
Risks: Single-asset dependence for the nation&apos;s entire crude output; a converted hull</description>
