				<name>Crude Processing &amp; Gathering Hubs</name>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Ulé Tank Farm (Tía Juana)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: PDVSA
Role: The gathering and storage point for crude produced across the Bolívar Coastal Fields — wells across Tía Juana and the neighbouring sub-fields feed their output here before it enters the pipeline system
Why it matters: This is the actual, named origin of the Ule-Amuay pipeline — &quot;Ulé&quot; is not a generic term, it is this specific tank farm, distinct from the La Salina/Bajo Grande terminals further south which serve Boscán&apos;s separate export route
Export route: Ule-Amuay Pipeline, 230 km north across the Gulf of Venezuela approach to the Paraguaná Refining Center
Risks: Sits within one of the world&apos;s most depleted oil basins; ageing storage and gathering infrastructure</description>
