				<Placemark>
					<name>Apiay Gathering Station (Meta)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Ecopetrol
Role: The gathering point near Villavicencio where Castilla and Chichimene crude enters Ecopetrol&apos;s pipeline grid, diluted with naphtha to reduce viscosity for transport
Why it matters: The Apiay-Porvenir pipeline leaving here has been flagged as the MAIN BOTTLENECK in Ecopetrol&apos;s Llanos evacuation infrastructure — getting the crude-naphtha dilution ratio right (targeting ~300 cSt viscosity) is an ongoing engineering constraint
Export route: Apiay-Porvenir pipeline toward the national grid, eventually reaching Monterrey/Vasconia and OCENSA
Risks: Chronic capacity constraint; heavy crude dilution requirements limit throughput</description>
