				<Placemark>
					<name>Dalian Oil Port</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Liaoning Port Group / Liaoning Port Co.; individual terminals, storage sites and pipelines operated with PetroChina/CNPC and other companies
Role: Northeast China’s principal seaborne oil gateway — receiving imported crude for refining, commercial and bonded storage, strategic reserves and regional redistribution
Main facilities: Xingang deep-water crude berths capable of receiving VLCC and larger tankers, crude and product terminals, extensive tank farms, strategic-storage sites and pipeline, rail, road and coastal-shipping connections
Connectivity: Supplies Dalian’s refining and storage cluster and connects maritime imports with the wider Liaoning, Jilin and Heilongjiang oil market; key grades include Russian ESPO and Middle Eastern crudes
Strategic role: The main intake and buffering point between international tanker routes and Northeast China’s refining system — allowing crude to be stored, blended, redirected or released from strategic reserves according to market conditions
Risks: Sanctions affecting Russian and Iranian crude flows; refinery closures or outages; pipeline and terminal accidents; oil spills; congestion and maritime disruption</description>
