				<Placemark>
					<name>Port of Fujairah</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Fujairah Ports Authority — Fujairah Oil Tanker Terminals (FOTT)
Role: Common marine interface connecting FOIZ storage terminals, refineries and processing plants with international crude, product and bunker markets
Infrastructure: 9 main or 14 wing oil berths; 330,000-DWT VLCC jetty; bunker-barge berths; piggable pipelines; two matrix-manifold systems
Connectivity: Directly connects participating FOIZ terminals to the oil berths and permits terminal-to-terminal transfers without chartering a vessel
Strategic role: The UAE’s principal liquid-bulk gateway outside the Strait of Hormuz and the physical foundation of the Fujairah bunkering and pricing hub
Risks: Concentration of tanks, pipelines and berths; Gulf of Oman security exposure; fire, spill and anchorage-congestion risk</description>
