				<Placemark>
					<name>Le Havre port</name>
					<description>Status: Operational

Owner/Operator: HAROPA PORT — French state public port authority

Role: Deepwater maritime gateway handling crude oil, refined petroleum products, petrochemicals, bunkers and other bulk cargoes entering the Lower Seine industrial system

Capacity: Multi-terminal port complex; oil-handling and storage capacity is distributed between dedicated terminals, tank farms and the neighbouring Normandy refining platform

Products: Crude oil, gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, fuel oil, marine fuels, petrochemical feedstocks and other liquid bulk products

Connectivity: Connected to the TotalEnergies Normandy refining platform, Le Havre and Antifer oil terminals, the TRAPIL Le Havre–Paris pipeline network, Seine barge transport, railways and major road corridors

Strategic role: Principal maritime oil gateway for the Lower Seine and Paris Basin, linking international tanker flows with refining, storage and fuel-distribution infrastructure serving northern France

Risks: Concentration of critical terminals and pipelines, industrial accidents, labour disruption, Channel and Seine navigation constraints, and declining long-term fossil-fuel demand</description>
