					</coordinates>
				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Escalante–Caleta Córdova Gathering Line</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Escalante Field, Golfo San Jorge Basin (Chubut) → Termap Caleta Córdova terminal, near Comodoro Rivadavia; a short local gathering line (~55 km), unlike the long cross-country trunks serving Vaca Muerta
Owner/Operator: PAE / Terminales Marítimas Patagónicas (Termap)
Role: Delivers Escalante crude directly from the field to its dedicated coastal export terminal — the Golfo San Jorge basin exports independently of the Oldelval/VMOS system, since its fields sit right on the Patagonian coast
Why it matters: Shows that not every Argentine crude flow needs a long trunk pipeline — Golfo San Jorge&apos;s chain is short and local because geography puts field and port side by side, unlike landlocked Vaca Muerta
Risks: A mature, high-water-cut basin under cost pressure; a single short line for the Escalante export stream</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
				<LineString>
					<tessellate>1</tessellate>
