				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Cañadón Seco–Caleta Olivia Gathering Line</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Cañadón Seco Field, Golfo San Jorge Basin (Santa Cruz) → Termap Caleta Olivia terminal; a short local gathering line (~13 km)
Owner/Operator: Field operators (including CGC, since acquiring former Sinopec concessions) / Termap
Role: Delivers Cañadón Seco crude directly from the field to its adjacent coastal export terminal, completing Golfo San Jorge&apos;s second, independent export chain
Why it matters: Confirms the pattern seen at Escalante — Golfo San Jorge&apos;s basin sits directly on the coast, so its value chain is field-to-port in a few kilometres, structurally different from the long inland-to-coast systems needed for Vaca Muerta
Risks: Mature field in a basin facing rising extraction costs relative to international crude prices</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
