					</coordinates>
				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Akal-C (Cantarell) – Dos Bocas Pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Akal-C platform, Cantarell Complex (Bay of Campeche, offshore) → Dos Bocas Marine Terminal, Tabasco; subsea then onshore delivery
Owner/Operator: Pemex
Role: The main gathering line bringing Mexico&apos;s flagship offshore crude — Cantarell/KMZ Maya and Isthmus streams — onshore for export or refining at the adjacent Olmeca refinery
Why it matters for exports: This is the physical link between Mexico&apos;s largest offshore fields and its main Gulf export terminal — the crude that eventually loads at Cayo Arcas or Dos Bocas travels this route first
Recent: Reported leaks (2025) briefly halted flow and caused a shoreline spill near Paraiso, Tabasco, underscoring the pipeline&apos;s central and singular role
Risks: Ageing subsea infrastructure; a single gathering line for Mexico&apos;s most important offshore crude</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
