				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Chain leg 1 — Enbridge Mainline (Hardisty–Superior)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Chain position: LEG 1 of 3 — Alberta to the US Great Lakes
Route: Trans Mountain Edmonton Terminal→ Hardisty / Edmonton (Alberta) → Regina → Cromer, Manitoba → Gretna border → Clearbrook, MN → Superior, Wisconsin
Owner/Operator: Enbridge (Mainline / Lakehead), ~3.1 million b/d across parallel Lines 1-4 and 67
Role: Carries the Western Canadian crude slate east to the Superior terminal, the pivot point where crude bound for Quebec transfers onto Line 5
Note: This is the same Enbridge Mainline mapped elsewhere; shown here as the first leg so the chain to Montreal is gapless
Next leg: at Superior, crude for Quebec moves onto Line 5</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
