				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Chain leg 2 — Enbridge Line 5 (Superior–Sarnia)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational since 1953 — contested (Michigan Straits of Mackinac litigation)
Chain position: LEG 2 of 3 — across the Great Lakes states to Ontario
Route: Superior, WI → Upper Peninsula of Michigan → under the Straits of Mackinac → Lower Michigan → across the St. Clair River → Sarnia, Ontario; 645 mi, up to 540,000 b/d
Owner/Operator: Enbridge
Role: The Great Lakes link — carries light crude, synthetic and NGLs from Superior to Sarnia. Without this leg, Line 9 (leg 3) has no crude source
Next leg: at Sarnia, crude for Quebec transfers onto Line 9
Risks: Straits of Mackinac shutdown risk; a tunnel replacement is planned</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
