					</coordinates>
				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Assaluyeh–Bandar Abbas Condensate Pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: South Pars Gas Complex at Assaluyeh → west of Bandar Abbas; 388 km along the Persian Gulf coast
Owner/Operator: National Iranian Oil Pipelines and Telecommunications Company
Capacity: Carries roughly 450,000 b/d of gas condensate
Role: The link that turns South Pars gas condensate into Iranian gasoline — without it, the Persian Gulf Star refinery has no feedstock and the condensate would have to be exported raw
Strategic role: Creates a self-contained southern fuel chain — offshore gas field, onshore separation at Assaluyeh, pipeline, condensate refinery, domestic fuel. Every step sits inside Iran, which matters under sanctions
Risks: A single line carrying the feedstock for 45% of national fuel supply; runs along an exposed coastal corridor</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
