					</coordinates>
				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>AB-4 Pipeline (Abqaiq–Sitra)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational — commissioned October 2018
Route: Saudi Aramco&apos;s Abqaiq plant → Sitra refinery, Bahrain; 115 km, of which 74 km overland and the remainder subsea across the Gulf
Owner/Operator: Saudi Aramco and Bapco jointly
Capacity: 350,000 b/d, replacing an ageing 230,000 b/d link
Role: The lifeline of Bahrain&apos;s refining industry — it carries the Saudi crude that makes up roughly five-sixths of Sitra&apos;s feedstock
History: Succeeds the original 1945 Dammam-Bahrain crude line, which was at the time the largest commercial underwater pipeline in the world
Strategic role: Built specifically to enable the Sitra refinery expansion; without it Bahrain&apos;s main export industry would have no feedstock
Risks: A single cross-border pipeline on which an entire national industry depends</description>
