				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>OCENSA Pipeline (Llanos–Coveñas)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Cusiana-Cupiagua area, Llanos Basin → Vasconia → Coveñas on the Caribbean coast; roughly 800 km
Owner/Operator: Cenit (Ecopetrol) with partner shareholders
Capacity: 615,000 b/d, historically running well below that
Role: Colombia&apos;s main export artery, carrying both Vasconia and Castilla Blend north to Coveñas — around 90% of the crude it delivers has gone to the United States
Connectivity: Collects the Rubiales line at Monterrey and the blended streams at Vasconia
Risks: Guerrilla and criminal attacks on pipeline infrastructure have been a recurring problem; underutilisation as Cusiana output declines</description>
