				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>SOTE Pipeline (Lago Agrio–Balao)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Lago Agrio, Oriente Basin → across the Andes → Balao terminal near Esmeraldas on the Pacific; ~500 km
Owner/Operator: Petroecuador
Capacity: 360,000-400,000 b/d, built 1970
Role: Carries the ORIENTE grade. Which pipeline a barrel enters is what determines its grade in Ecuador — SOTE crude becomes Oriente, OCP crude becomes Napo
Recent: Ruptured by Andean landslides in 2003 and on later occasions, forcing force majeure and emergency use of the OCP line
Risks: Crosses seismically active, landslide-prone Andean slopes; a single corridor for the state&apos;s entire export stream</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
