					</coordinates>
				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>ESPO Skovorodino–Daqing Spur (China)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Skovorodino → Amur River border crossing → Mohe → Daqing, Heilongjiang; 64-67 km in Russia plus roughly 960-1,000 km in China
Owner/Operator: Transneft on the Russian side; CNPC on the Chinese side
Capacity: 300,000 b/d under the 20-year oil-for-loan agreement between Transneft, Rosneft and CNPC
Role: The overland branch of the ESPO system, delivering crude straight into China&apos;s northern refining network at Daqing
Strategic role: The only major Russian crude export route with no seaborne leg at all — immune to tanker sanctions, insurance restrictions and maritime interdiction, which has made it strategically central since 2022
Risks: Single-customer dependence on China, which holds the pricing power; cross-border tariff and contract renegotiation risk</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
				<LineString>
					<tessellate>1</tessellate>
