			<Placemark>
				<name>Omsk–Samara Pipeline (West Siberia → Volga)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Omsk → across the southern Urals → Samara/Kuibyshev in the Volga region
Owner/Operator: Transneft
Role: The westward continuation from Omsk, carrying West Siberian crude to the Volga crossroads where the European export routes begin
Onward routes: At Samara the stream divides toward the Baltic, the Black Sea or Druzhba
Why it matters: The trunk that physically links Russia&apos;s main producing basin to its European export outlets — the spine of the Urals system
Alignment: schematic — the junction and its connections are documented, the drawn corridor is indicative</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
				<LineString>
					<tessellate>1</tessellate>
