				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Omsk–Taishet Pipeline (West Siberia → ESPO)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Omsk, West Siberia → Taishet, the head of the ESPO system (the historic Omsk–Irkutsk trunk)
Owner/Operator: Transneft
Role: The physical link that lets WEST Siberian crude reach the EASTERN export system — without it, ESPO would depend solely on East Siberian fields, which cannot fill it
Strategic role: This is the junction where Russia chooses east or west. Barrels arriving at Taishet can go to Kozmino and China, or stay in the western grid and be sold as Urals. Diverting the sweeter West Siberian streams eastward is what has degraded Urals quality for European refiners
Risks: A single connector carrying the flexibility of the entire export system; any outage forces crude back into the western market</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
				<LineString>
