					</coordinates>
				</LineString>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Purpe–Samotlor Pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Purpe, Yamal-Nenets region → Samotlor, Khanty-Mansi region; roughly 430 km
Owner/Operator: Transneft
Role: Connects the Arctic Zapolyarye–Purpe line into the main Transneft trunk network at Samotlor, from where crude can travel west to the Baltic and Black Sea or east via Omsk–Taishet into ESPO
Strategic role: The missing link in the Arctic chain — Zapolyarye–Purpe brings far-northern crude south, but only this segment puts it into the grid where it becomes part of Urals or ESPO
Risks: Permafrost construction; a single corridor carrying the whole northern Yamal onshore stream</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
