			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Samara–Tikhoretsk–Novorossiysk Trunk (southern export route)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Samara/Kuibyshev → Volgograd → Tikhoretsk → Novorossiysk (Sheskharis terminal) on the Black Sea
Owner/Operator: Transneft
Role: Russia&apos;s southern crude export corridor, feeding the Sheskharis terminal at Novorossiysk — the Black Sea counterpart to Primorsk and Ust-Luga on the Baltic
Onward routes: Seaborne export through the Bosphorus, plus a branch to the Tuapse refinery
Recent: A 2013 rupture near Volgograd halted Novorossiysk crude exports entirely until repairs were completed, showing how much depends on this single corridor
Why it matters: Without this line, Sheskharis and the Novorossiysk export complex have no crude supply — it was the missing link between Russia&apos;s producing regions and its Black Sea outlet
Alignment: schematic — the junction and its connections are documented, the drawn corridor is indicative</description>
