			<Placemark>
				<name>Surgut–Polotsk Trunk (West Siberia → Belarus)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Surgut, West Siberia → across the Urals and central Russia → Polotsk/Novopolotsk, Belarus; roughly 3,250 km
Owner/Operator: Transneft
Role: A direct West Siberia to Belarus trunk, separate from the Druzhba corridor — it is the supply line for the Naftan refinery at Novopolotsk
Why it matters: Explains how Naftan is fed. Belarus has two refineries served by two different routes: Mozyr from Druzhba via Unecha, and Naftan from West Siberia via this line. Transneft has confirmed that while parallel corridors were converted to diesel service, Surgut–Polotsk continues pumping crude for export
Recent: Transit to the Baltic states via this corridor ceased in 2006; the line now serves Belarus
Alignment: schematic — endpoints and route cities are documented, the drawn corridor is indicative</description>
