			<Placemark>
				<name>Ust-Balyk–Omsk Pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Ust-Balyk (Nefteyugansk area) → Omsk; crosses the Irtysh floodplain
Owner/Operator: Transneft Siberia
Role: Carries West Siberian crude out of the Nefteyugansk–Samotlor production area to Omsk, the hinge between the western and eastern systems
Onward routes: From Omsk, crude can go west toward Samara and the European outlets, or east on the Omsk–Taishet line into ESPO
Why it matters: One of the oldest and most heavily used Soviet-era trunk lines, and the first leg of the journey for most Urals-bound crude
Alignment: schematic — the junction and its connections are documented, the drawn corridor is indicative</description>
