			<Placemark>
				<name>Brent System Pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Brent field, East Shetland Basin → Sullom Voe terminal, Shetland; ~154 km, 36-inch
Owner/Operator: Shell UK
Handles: Brent crude, blended with Ninian volumes at Sullom Voe into Brent/Ninian Blend (BNB) — a Dated Brent basket grade
Connectivity: Also carries third-party volumes from surrounding East Shetland Basin fields as Brent&apos;s own output has collapsed
Strategic role: The line that carried the crude the global benchmark is named after; Brent field output is now around 23,000 b/d, roughly one cargo a month
Risks: Throughput now depends largely on third-party tie-ins rather than the namesake field; Brent platform decommissioning under way</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
