			<Placemark>
				<name>Buzzard–Forties Pipeline Tie-in</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Buzzard field → tie-in to the Forties Pipeline System, central North Sea
Owner/Operator: CNOOC International
Handles: Buzzard crude at ~32.6° API and 1.44% sulfur — heavier and markedly sourer than the Forties stream it joins
Strategic role: The single most consequential tie-in on the UK shelf for benchmark quality. INEOS publishes a live table showing Forties Blend ranging from 43.3° API / 0.29% sulfur at 0% Buzzard content to 36.6° API / 1.01% sulfur at 60% — so the flow through this short connector changes the specification of a Dated Brent basket grade week to week
Risks: Buzzard outages are directly visible in Dated Brent quality and pricing</description>
