			<Placemark>
				<name>Clair Pipeline (West of Shetland)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Clair and Clair Ridge platforms, West of Shetland → Sullom Voe terminal; ~105 km
Owner/Operator: BP
Handles: Clair crude — heavy at ~23° API, kept as its own assessed grade rather than blended into BNB
Strategic role: Connects the Atlantic margin, where the UK&apos;s remaining reserve base sits, back to the mature Shetland terminal infrastructure built for the Brent era
Risks: Harsh Atlantic-margin conditions; long-term reliance on an ageing terminal designed for a different production profile</description>
