			<Placemark>
				<name>Grane Oil Pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Grane field (Utsira High) → Sture Terminal; ~212 km, 29-inch
Owner/Operator: Equinor (Gassco as system operator)
Capacity: Around 500,000 b/d
Handles: Grane Blend — a heavier, more sulphurous Norwegian stream (~27° API, 0.67% sulfur) than the basket grades, kept separate from Oseberg at Sture
Connectivity: Shares the Sture Terminal with the Oseberg system, which is why Sture loads two distinct grades
Risks: Heavy-crude economics; shared terminal dependence with Oseberg</description>
