			<Placemark>
				<name>Johan Sverdrup Oil Pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Johan Sverdrup field centre (Utsira High) → Mongstad terminal; ~283 km, 36-inch
Owner/Operator: Equinor
Capacity: Sized for the field&apos;s full plateau, toward 755,000 b/d
Handles: Johan Sverdrup crude — the largest single North Sea stream, medium sour at ~28° API and 0.81% sulfur, deliberately excluded from the Dated Brent basket
Strategic role: The pipeline that physically delivered the North Sea&apos;s shift from light sweet to medium sour; its volumes now rival major OPEC grades into Asia
Risks: Single-line dependence for the region&apos;s biggest field; Mongstad terminal concentration</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
