			<Placemark>
				<name>Ninian Pipeline System</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Ninian Central platform → Sullom Voe terminal, Shetland; ~177 km, 36-inch
Owner/Operator: CNR International
Handles: Ninian crude, commingled with Brent at Sullom Voe to form Brent/Ninian Blend
Strategic role: As Brent&apos;s own volumes have declined, Ninian has become essential to keeping BNB cargoes at viable size — which is why Platts names the assessed grade after both fields
Risks: Mature field base; the viability of the whole BNB stream depends on combined Brent and Ninian throughput</description>
