			<Placemark>
				<name>Norpipe Oil Pipeline (Ekofisk–Teesside)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Ekofisk complex (Norwegian North Sea) → Teesside terminal, north-east England; ~354 km, 34-inch
Owner/Operator: Gassco as system operator, with ConocoPhillips as technical service provider
Capacity: Design capacity around 900,000 b/d; onstream since 1975
Handles: Ekofisk Blend, gathering the Greater Ekofisk Area — Ekofisk, Eldfisk, Embla and Tor — plus third-party tie-ins
Strategic role: The only major Norwegian crude stream that reaches market by pipeline to another country rather than by tanker from a Norwegian terminal — Norwegian crude landing on UK soil
Risks: Single-corridor dependence for the whole Ekofisk area; ageing line in service five decades; cross-border regulatory exposure</description>
