			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>Oseberg Transport System (OTS)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Oseberg Field Centre → Sture Terminal, Øygarden; ~115 km, 28-inch
Owner/Operator: Equinor (Gassco as system operator)
Capacity: Around 900,000 b/d
Handles: Oseberg Blend — a Dated Brent (BFOET) basket grade, so this line carries crude that can set the global benchmark
Connectivity: Also receives third-party volumes from surrounding Norwegian fields before landfall at Sture
Strategic role: One of the physical arteries feeding the Dated Brent basket; the Norwegian counterpart to the UK&apos;s Forties Pipeline System
Risks: Concentrates a benchmark-setting grade on one line and one terminal</description>
