			<Placemark>
				<name>Gialo-Waha pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Gialo oil field → Waha oil field/processing hub → onward to the Es Sider export terminal, Sirte Basin, Libya; 152 km, 30-inch line
Owner/Operator: Waha Oil Company — Libya&apos;s NOC 59.2%, TotalEnergies 16.3%, ConocoPhillips 16.3% (Total and ConocoPhillips bought out Hess&apos;s former 8.2% stake in 2021)
Capacity: ~20 million t/yr nameplate; carries the Gialo, Samah and Dahra field streams that make up Libya&apos;s Es Sider benchmark grade
Recent: Repeated leaks and shutdowns — an 18 km section replaced in 2019; a 2021 leak cut Gialo output by 60,000-70,000 b/d; Waha&apos;s fields typically run 280,000-300,000 b/d into an Es Sider export stream of roughly 260,000-350,000 b/d
Risks: Ageing, war-affected infrastructure; recurring leaks and maintenance shutdowns; single-corridor dependence for Waha&apos;s output reaching Es Sider</description>
				<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin</styleUrl>
