			<Placemark>
				<name>Trans Mountain Pipeline</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Edmonton, Alberta → Rockies → Kamloops/Merritt → Westridge Marine Terminal, Burnaby, BC
Owner: Trans Mountain Corporation — Government of Canada (since 2018)
Capacity: Two parallel lines — legacy (1953, 300,000 b/d) + TMX (2024, 590,000 b/d) = 890,000 b/d total, running 87-95% utilisation
Strategic role: Canada&apos;s only crude pipeline to tidewater — opened Asian/US West Coast markets, easing dependence on US-bound Enbridge/Keystone routes
Risks: Near-full utilisation; mountainous/Indigenous-land sensitivity; sole Pacific-coast outlet for Canadian crude</description>
