					</LineString>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Fujairah &amp; Gulf of Oman Pricing Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Role: The East-of-Suez crude and bunkering pricing zone — outside the Strait of Hormuz, which 2026 turned from convenience into consecration
Why it&apos;s a major hub: Fujairah combines three separate functions at one port that most locations only have one of — a physically-settled crude futures contract, the region&apos;s benchmark bunker fuel market, and a weekly inventory signal the whole Gulf watches
Benchmark instruments:
— ICE Murban Futures (IFAD): launched March 2021 on ICE Futures Abu Dhabi, the first futures contract based on Murban crude — ADNOC&apos;s flagship export grade. Exchange-traded and physically settled, delivered here rather than cash-settled, which is what makes it directly comparable to WTI at Cushing rather than to a pure paper instrument like a swap
— Platts Fujairah bunker assessments: the world&apos;s reference bunker fuel prices for ships transiting the region
— FOIZ weekly inventory data: the Gulf&apos;s most-watched stock signal, tracking crude, products and fuel oil held in the FOIZ tank farms
Physical basis: Port of Fujairah; the ADCOP pipeline terminus, which brings Murban crude here from Habshan, bypassing the Strait of Hormuz entirely; the FOIZ tank farms; one of the world&apos;s busiest bunkering anchorages
Recent: 2026 — the working price point of a closed-strait world: bunker demand, storage value and Murban&apos;s non-Hormuz delivery route all gained weight simultaneously
Strategic role: Where the Gulf&apos;s oil gets priced when the Gulf itself is shut — Murban&apos;s whole strategic premise is that it never has to transit Hormuz to be delivered
Risks: Tanker incidents (2019 precedent); anchorage congestion; dependence on ADCOP throughput; Murban&apos;s liquidity still trails Brent and WTI despite its structural advantage</description>
					<styleUrl>#hub1011</styleUrl>
					<LineString>
						<tessellate>1</tessellate>
						<coordinates>
