				<Placemark>
					<name>Platts Dubai (Physical Assessment)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Type: Regional physical price assessment
Function: Prices Middle East sour crude sold to Asia — the region&apos;s oldest and most widely referenced benchmark
Mechanism: Assessed daily by S&amp;P Global Platts through the Market-on-Close process. Originally based only on Dubai&apos;s own Fateh field; since 2016 the deliverable basket has widened to five grades — Dubai, Oman, Upper Zakum, Al-Shaheen and Murban
Why here: Fateh remains the symbolic and historical home of the assessment, even though the physical barrels behind it now mostly come from elsewhere
Risks: A benchmark whose namesake field barely produces; credibility now rests entirely on the four other grades in the basket</description>
