				<Placemark>
					<name>NYMEX ULSD / Heating Oil Futures (HO), New York Harbor</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Type: Exchange-traded, physically-settled futures — the US middle-distillate benchmark
Function: Hedging and price discovery for diesel and heating oil; the direct US counterpart to Europe&apos;s ICE Low Sulphur Gasoil contract
Mechanism: Traded on NYMEX/CME (symbol HO), physically delivered in New York Harbor. Originally the &quot;Heating Oil&quot; contract, respecified to ultra-low-sulfur diesel (ULSD) to match modern fuel standards
Relationship to other benchmarks: Traders use the &quot;heating oil crack&quot; (HO minus WTI) to hedge refining margins on the distillate side — one of the most-watched refining spreads in the US, the mirror of Europe&apos;s gasoil crack
Why here: New York Harbor is the contract&apos;s delivery basis — the US Northeast products and import hub, a distinct pricing location from the crude points at Cushing and Houston
Risks: Northeast demand is seasonal (heating oil); competition from renewable diesel; a delivery basis on the demand coast rather than the producing region</description>
