				<Placemark>
					<name>NYMEX RBOB Gasoline Futures (RB), New York Harbor</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Type: Exchange-traded, physically-settled futures — the US gasoline benchmark
Function: Hedging and price discovery for gasoline; the reference contract for US motor-fuel prices
Mechanism: Traded on NYMEX/CME (symbol RB). RBOB = Reformulated Blendstock for Oxygenate Blending — the gasoline component delivered before ethanol is splash-blended in. Physically delivered in New York Harbor
Relationship to other benchmarks: The &quot;RBOB crack&quot; (RB minus WTI) hedges the gasoline side of refining margins; combined with the heating-oil crack it defines the US 3-2-1 crack spread (3 barrels crude → 2 gasoline + 1 distillate), the standard shorthand for US refinery profitability
Why here: New York Harbor delivery basis — the same US Northeast products hub as the ULSD contract, which is why this circle sits alongside it
Risks: Seasonal demand (summer driving season); the ethanol-blending structure adds basis complexity; shifting gasoline demand as EV adoption grows</description>
