				<Placemark>
					<name>ICE Murban Futures (Fujairah)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Type: Exchange-traded, physically-settled futures — grade-specific, unlike GME Oman which delivers a blended stream
Function: Murban/UAE crude exposure — hedging and price discovery for ADNOC&apos;s flagship export grade
Mechanism: Traded on ICE Futures Abu Dhabi (IFAD), launched March 2021 as the first futures contract based on Murban crude. Physically delivered at Fujairah, outside the Strait of Hormuz on the Gulf of Oman coast
Why here: Fujairah is the contract&apos;s actual, named delivery point — the same location as this map&apos;s broader Fujairah &amp; Gulf of Oman Major Energy Hub, but this entry represents the specific tradeable instrument rather than the hub&apos;s overall role
Why it matters: Murban settling outside Hormuz gave it a strategic advantage during 2026&apos;s strait tensions — a non-Hormuz-exposed physically-delivered benchmark became more attractive precisely when Gulf transit risk rose
Risks: Newer and less liquid than Brent or WTI; competes with GME Oman and Platts Dubai for the same East-of-Suez pricing role</description>
