				<Placemark>
					<name>GME Oman Crude Oil Futures (Mina al-Fahal)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Type: Exchange-traded, physically-settled futures
Function: Oman/Middle East price discovery and hedging — the only Middle East sour crude futures contract settled by actual physical delivery
Mechanism: Launched 2007 as DME Oman on the Dubai Mercantile Exchange; renamed GME (Gulf Mercantile Exchange) 2 September 2024. Physical delivery at Mina al-Fahal, settled daily at the close of Singapore trading
Why it matters: Saudi Aramco adopted GME Oman for its Asia pricing formula in 2018, followed by Bahrain and Kuwait
Risks: Physical delivery concentrated at one Omani terminal; liquidity still smaller than Brent or WTI</description>
