				<name>Independent Storage Terminals</name>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Vopak Terminal Algeciras</name>
					<description>Status: Operational since 2013
Owner/Operator: Vopak (80%), Vilma Oil (20%), via the Alpetrol concession from Algeciras Port Authority
Role: The first INDEPENDENT (third-party) oil storage terminal in Algeciras — distinct from any refinery, offering storage services to traders and other customers rather than one captive owner
Capacity: 403,000 m3 across 22 tanks, with a jetty able to take vessels up to 225,000 dwt
Why here: Independent commercial storage, the same category as Vopak&apos;s other global terminals on this map (Fujairah, ARA) — capitalising on Algeciras&apos;s position as a major bunkering and transhipment hub at the Strait of Gibraltar
Risks: Competitive independent-storage market; exposure to regional bunker-fuel demand cycles</description>
