				<Placemark>
					<name>Keyera / Kinder Morgan Edmonton Storage Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Keyera and Kinder Morgan (joint venture), operated by Kinder Morgan
Role: A large independent above-ground crude storage terminal in the Edmonton cluster — 12 tanks providing 4.8 million barrels of capacity, with room for 1.8 million more
Connectivity: Pipeline-connected to Kinder Morgan&apos;s existing Edmonton storage and to all crude streams it handles; customers can deliver onward via major pipelines and the nearby Keyera and Kinder Morgan rail terminals
Role in the chain: Commercial storage and blending flexibility at the pipeline-origin hub — where shippers stage crude before it enters the Mainline, Trans Mountain or rail systems
Why here: Part of the dense Edmonton/Strathcona tank-farm cluster (with the Trans Mountain, Enbridge, Suncor and Keyera terminals) that is the staging yard for Canada&apos;s entire crude-export system
Risks: Serves a single concentrated hub; storage-margin cycles</description>
