				<Placemark>
					<name>HES Wilhelmshaven Tank Terminal (Voslapper Groden)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: HES Wilhelmshaven Tank Terminal GmbH (HWTT), a subsidiary of HES International — formerly the ConocoPhillips Wilhelmshaven refinery site, bought by Hestya Energy and converted to a storage terminal
Role: A large independent third-party liquids storage terminal on the Voslapper Groden at Wilhelmshaven, with its own deep-water berths — the huge diked tank groups in the screenshot
Capacity: ~1.3 million m3 of tank storage, handling crude and products
Processing twist: Retains a 2.5 million t/yr LOW-SULFUR FUEL OIL (LSFO) production unit — a revamped vacuum distillation unit from the old refinery that now turns low-sulfur crude into IMO-2020-compliant marine fuel, giving the terminal a rare storage-plus-processing role
Distinction: Separate from the neighbouring NWO crude terminal (which feeds the Gelsenkirchen pipeline) — Wilhelmshaven hosts multiple large tank terminals side by side
Why here: Independent (fee-based) storage with berths, the same category as Vopak, BOSTCO and Zenith elsewhere on this map
Risks: European storage-margin and bunker-demand cycles; a converted refinery site</description>
