				<Placemark>
					<name>Scholven Tank Farm (Tanklager, Gelsenkirchen)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Ruhr Oel GmbH-Gelsenkirchen (Klesch), fed by the NWO pipeline system
Role: The pipeline-connected crude and product tank farm serving the Scholven refinery — the buffer storage between the NWO pipeline from Wilhelmshaven and the refinery units
Why it matters (2026 low-Rhine story): S&amp;P Global Energy CERA notes that while other Rhine refineries struggle when water levels hit critical lows, GELSENKIRCHEN can still access crude through this nearby, PIPELINE-CONNECTED Scholven tank facility — it is supplied by pipe, not by river barge, so it is insulated from the Rhine low-water disruption that cripples barge-dependent sites
Connectivity: Receives crude via the NWO (Nord-West Oelleitung) pipeline from the Wilhelmshaven deep-water import terminal on the North Sea
Risks: Depends on the single NWO pipeline corridor; ageing storage infrastructure</description>
