				<Placemark>
					<name>Kinder Morgan Carson / Los Angeles Harbor Terminals</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Kinder Morgan
Role: Fee-based independent storage terminals near the Los Angeles-basin refineries — the Carson terminal and the connected Los Angeles Harbor terminal, storing crude, black oil and refined products
Capacity: Part of Kinder Morgan&apos;s West Coast terminal system totalling nearly 8 million barrels
Connectivity: Connected to numerous pipelines and facilities across the LA area, giving customers flexibility to respond quickly to market conditions; storage arranged mainly on 1-5 year term contracts
Why here: Third-party rented storage, distinct from refinery-owned tankage
Risks: Serves a shrinking refinery base; competition from other LA-basin independents (Vopak, Zenith)</description>
