					<name>Kinder Morgan Richmond Terminal (San Francisco Bay)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Kinder Morgan
Role: The principal independent storage and distribution terminal in Northern California — chemicals, lubricants and paraffin waxes, and the main point through which tropical oils are imported and US vegetable oils exported to the Far East
Connectivity: San Francisco Bay marine access; serves the Northern California market alongside the Chevron Richmond refinery nearby
Why here: Third-party fee-based storage, distinct from the adjacent refinery
Risks: Bay-area environmental scrutiny; niche chemical/specialty focus</description>
