				<Placemark>
					<name>BOSTCO Terminal (Bayport, Houston Ship Channel)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Oiltanking / Enterprise (Battleground Oil Specialty Terminal Company)
Role: A large independent third-party storage terminal on the Houston Ship Channel at Bayport, specialising in black oil, residual fuel, distillates and bunker feedstocks
Capacity: Over 7 million barrels across large above-ground tanks, with deep-water ship docks and a barge dock
Function: Rented tankage for traders and refiners — storage and blending of heavy products and fuel oil, not a producer-owned facility
Why here: Third-party commercial storage, the same category as Vopak and the ARA independent tank farms — distinct from the captive terminals attached to refineries
Risks: Ship Channel congestion; product-market demand swings for residual fuel</description>
