				<Placemark id="0E6E8239333F9FF0FF11">
					<name>Geneva fuel infrastructure</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Location: Vernier, Canton of Geneva — Switzerland&apos;s largest concentration of fuel storage tanks (around 125), operated by multiple companies, with Tamoil running the country&apos;s largest depot network here
Role: Receives refined products via the SPMR pipeline from Fos-sur-Mer through Feyzin (Lyon), supplying the whole canton of Geneva and part of the Vaud/Lake Geneva region; also holds part of Switzerland&apos;s compulsory strategic fuel reserves
Risks: A dense urban population sits directly next to this Seveso high-threshold tank farm, driving repeated local political pressure to relocate or reduce tank numbers; single-pipeline dependence on the Fos-Feyzin-Vernier corridor</description>
