				<Placemark id="0DD541FB773F9FFBE1F4">
					<name>Le Havre port storage (France)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Role: The tank-storage side of Le Havre&apos;s oil complex, distinct from the port infrastructure entry — historically the origin point of TotalEnergies&apos; Île-de-France crude pipeline (PLIF) to the Grandpuits refinery, and still a hub for TRAPIL&apos;s Le Havre-Paris (LHP) refined-products pipeline network supplying the Paris region and Roissy/Orly airports
Recent: The crude PLIF pipeline&apos;s future has been uncertain since TotalEnergies stopped processing crude at Grandpuits in 2021 and began converting it into a biofuel/multi-energy platform; the refined-product LHP network continues to operate
Risks: Ageing infrastructure (PLIF dates to 1968, with a multi-month outage in 2019); questions over long-term throughput following Grandpuits&apos; shift away from crude refining</description>
