				<Placemark>
					<name>Universal Terminal (Jurong Island)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Jurong Port 41% (took over the Lim family/Hin Leong stake in 2021), PetroChina International (Singapore) 25%, MAIF Investments Singapore (Macquarie) 34%
Role: The largest independent petroleum storage terminal in Asia-Pacific — a trading and blending hub used by international oil majors and trading houses, not tied to any single national export flow
Capacity: ~2.33-2.5 million m³ across 15 jetties, including two VLCC berths and nine bunker barge berths; also holds exclusive access to Southeast Asia&apos;s first underground rock-cavern oil storage facility
Recent: Restructured in 2021 after former major shareholder Hin Leong Trading collapsed with roughly $4 billion in debt; connected to neighbouring Horizon Singapore Terminals by a new fuel-oil and clean-products pipeline completed in 2024
Risks: Concentrated ownership among a small group of investors following the Hin Leong collapse; a single point of failure for a large share of Singapore&apos;s merchant storage capacity</description>
