					<name>Vopak Sebarok Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Royal Vopak, in partnership with PSA International; Singapore&apos;s first independent third-party oil storage terminal, opened 1983
Role: A dedicated fuel-oil and gasoil blending and bunkering hub on its own island, close to Singapore&apos;s Eastern bunkering anchorage
Capacity: Roughly 1.3 million m³ (8.4 million barrels) across 83 tanks, with 9 vessel berths and a 17.6 m draught allowing vessels up to 210,000 DWT
Connectivity: Offers concurrent bunkering — vessels can receive bunkers while simultaneously loading or discharging cargo — to speed up vessel turnaround
Risks: Standalone-island logistics entirely dependent on ferry/barge access; concentrates a large share of fuel-oil blending activity in one location</description>
