						<name>Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta International Airport</name>
						<description>Status: Operational
Role: The world&apos;s busiest airport by passenger traffic; Delta Air Lines&apos; primary hub
Fuel relevance: Supplied by US Gulf Coast refining capacity via pipeline and rail — the largest single concentration of jet-fuel demand tied to the Gulf Coast refining row already on this map
Connectivity: The Colonial Pipeline system is the primary jet-fuel artery from the Gulf Coast to Atlanta
Risks: Heavy reliance on one pipeline corridor for the bulk of its fuel supply</description>
