					<Placemark>
						<name>London Heathrow Airport</name>
						<description>Status: Operational
Role: The UK&apos;s largest airport and Europe&apos;s busiest by passenger numbers; British Airways&apos; main hub
Fuel relevance: Supplied via the UK Oil Pipelines Organisation (UKOP) network from Thames/Essex refining and import terminals, also drawing on North Sea-linked product flows
Connectivity: A dedicated pipeline links coastal import terminals directly to the airport
Risks: Concentrated dependence on a small number of UK import terminals; long-running capacity and expansion constraints</description>
						<styleUrl>#msn_icon?color=1976d2&amp;id=2000&amp;scale=440001</styleUrl>
