			<Folder>
				<name>Military air bases</name>
				<Placemark id="07A2E4942F3F60CB6ECD">
					<name>Ramstein Air Base</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Role: The largest US Air Force base outside the United States — a key logistics and refuelling hub for US military operations across Europe, the Middle East and Africa
Fuel relevance: Represents military jet-fuel demand, generally separate from commercial supply chains — typically supplied via the NATO pipeline system already mapped
Connectivity: Directly tied to the NATO pipeline network on this map, built during the Cold War specifically to supply US and allied air bases in Germany
Risks: Strategic/security sensitivity; fuel logistics tied to military rather than commercial market dynamics</description>
